.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/8e022d3c49e158d4a1b8e7858686bb6fe26b3970/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:50:42Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:50:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix stale relation table in field widget when switching records in side panel (#22829)\n\nThe relation table rendered by a FIELD widget in TABLE display mode kept\nits jotai component states (loaded rows, virtualization maps, loading\nguards, query identifiers) in instances keyed only by widget id and view\nid. Since the side panel record pages share those instances across\nrecords, switching to another record kept rendering the previous\nrecord''s related rows until an asynchronous catch-up reload landed, and\nany race or error in that catch-up left the previous record''s data on\nscreen permanently.\n\nScope the record-table widget''s context store instance and record index\ninstance by target record id (and side panel surface), the same way\nFieldsWidget already scopes its field list instances. Each record now\ngets its own table state, so a record''s rows can never appear under\nanother record, and loads that land after a record switch write into\ntheir own instance instead of the visible one.\n\nloadRecordIndexStates and setRecordGroupsFromViewGroups accept an\noptional recordIndexId override so the widget view load effect can\npopulate the record-scoped instance instead of deriving the shared one\nfrom object name and view id.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22829?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"b816e7fb476b26267031adddbb79a686acd53fea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/b816e7fb476b26267031adddbb79a686acd53fea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/8e022d3c49e158d4a1b8e7858686bb6fe26b3970","verification":{"payload":"tree b816e7fb476b26267031adddbb79a686acd53fea\nparent b2a4bb0e0c9bef64ba6a0ef2e97a788827d165ec\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1783947042 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783947042 +0200\n\nFix stale relation table in field widget when switching records in side panel (#22829)\n\nThe relation table rendered by a FIELD widget in TABLE display mode kept\nits jotai component states (loaded rows, virtualization maps, loading\nguards, query identifiers) in instances keyed only by widget id and view\nid. Since the side panel record pages share those instances across\nrecords, switching to another record kept rendering the previous\nrecord''s related rows until an asynchronous catch-up reload landed, and\nany race or error in that catch-up left the previous record''s data on\nscreen permanently.\n\nScope the record-table widget''s context store instance and record index\ninstance by target record id (and side panel surface), the same way\nFieldsWidget already scopes its field list instances. Each record now\ngets its own table state, so a record''s rows can never appear under\nanother record, and loads that land after a record switch write into\ntheir own instance instead of the visible one.\n\nloadRecordIndexStates and setRecordGroupsFromViewGroups accept an\noptional recordIndexId override so the widget view load effect can\npopulate the record-scoped instance instead of deriving the shared one\nfrom object name and view id.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22829?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVN8iCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEq4QAK8UV928BL2Uh8PCsNHFn+QO\n7qOS4+Kv7dMyiOdvweXwXxYHnTh7rVz2K5mzXmy7JniWOgqDc5QceKTlouoj1zdT\n/sdsHUVs+mJfYLZpcuKMzIKavcQ2StCGx1JB05DlzFlhYnLzyoOkj3wd4m/4aqgP\nT7zOGFVz0n3AA/dFrWrKzcYwtrF5j53GS9o8H/n6MFMmhGY28fULlR0ksQzKgD5w\nYQfIcH1cNlfKN9fQLNd3IWdUNMrr6qy74NvLCnU0GGMNbJCnrE1AYOBduhV0D/q8\nrF7SlsmFfJwezU7gY+1+H+DyPd7vaH6g/HK6FfsVvGy7QcWpvpgTn4fARHSSGDEQ\n7JXozDsRMViKKwZrk20vtTvoh4aVwmJBcbxgIzcuqMb/vobwSo1TcRLKH9u3oof0\n5gDTDVaAa/OjwDeZDAOhxjckrxV9Ok1IqElygGcVXc5LJtDmPUeIV7aUpf7rfQIH\ntNoG8K/kM+S3WIAQIVkkyjuhBaP1EdJ1iuJ+iNXW6fRiTkg055NMD8bhALvquvj+\nk0o9kbp8WQVoN+bz9KmEi9nFC+atbI3O7/OIfUp2jwnVptW0gywoWL5vCDKymG7k\nL3GleXgS5YdJ+7X0FfC+m/1lis3GqLi00h/ulnI1PfDbKIDXDJWAr/QbDtd1ihSJ\n/P+3HCDo3BjMmxoc2qjR\n=+OXT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:14:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/8e022d3c49e158d4a1b8e7858686bb6fe26b3970","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKDhlMDIyZDNjNDllMTU4ZDRhMWI4ZTc4NTg2ODZiYjZmZTI2YjM5NzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/b2a4bb0e0c9bef64ba6a0ef2e97a788827d165ec","sha":"b2a4bb0e0c9bef64ba6a0ef2e97a788827d165ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/b2a4bb0e0c9bef64ba6a0ef2e97a788827d165ec"}],"sha":"8e022d3c49e158d4a1b8e7858686bb6fe26b3970","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/8e022d3c49e158d4a1b8e7858686bb6fe26b3970"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45004772?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prastoin","id":45004772,"login":"prastoin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA0Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/b2a4bb0e0c9bef64ba6a0ef2e97a788827d165ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:39:06Z","email":"45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paul Rastoin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:39:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(apps): add Targeting System Fields page (#22856)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a docs page teaching app developers how to reference auto-created\n**system fields** (`createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `id`, …) from views and\nother entities, and makes the API it documents real by exporting\n`generateDefaultFieldUniversalIdentifier` from the SDK.\n\n## Why\n\nSystem fields are provisioned by the server, so they''re never declared\nwith `defineField()` and have no importable `universalIdentifier`\nconstant. Since 2.19 their universal identifier is derived\ndeterministically from the application id, the object id and the field\nname. Hardcoding an invented id fails sync with `INVALID_VIEW_DATA:\nField metadata not found` (this is exactly what broke the\ntwenty-partners `createdAt` view column).\n\nThe twenty-partners app already imports\n`generateDefaultFieldUniversalIdentifier` from `twenty-sdk/define`, but\nthe function was never exported from the SDK. This PR adds the export\nand documents the pattern.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **New page** `data/system-fields.mdx` — \"Targeting System Fields\":\n- Lists the 8 system fields (`id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`,\n`deletedAt`, `createdBy`, `updatedBy`, `position`, `searchVector`).\n- Explains the deterministic derivation and the sync error from\nhardcoding ids.\n- Documents `generateDefaultFieldUniversalIdentifier({\napplicationUniversalIdentifier, objectUniversalIdentifier, fieldName })`\nwith a full `defineView` example.\n- Contrasts with standard objects (use\n`STANDARD_OBJECT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS.<object>.fields.<field>.universalIdentifier`)\nand notes that `name` is a default, not system, field.\n- **SDK export** — new `generate-default-field-universal-identifier.ts`\nwrapping the existing `getFieldUniversalIdentifier` from\n`twenty-shared/application` (`name` → `fieldName`), exported from\n`define/index.ts`.\n- Registered the page in `docs.json` (Data group) and cross-linked it\nfrom the Views doc.\n\n## Notes\n\n`node_modules` isn''t installed in this environment, so `nx typecheck`\nwasn''t run. The wrapper is a signature-matched pass-through and the\n`twenty-shared/application` subpath + `getFieldUniversalIdentifier`\nbarrel export were both verified to exist.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_017B7VivHcqZYjn3ukestY9U)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22856?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions <github-actions@twenty.com>","tree":{"sha":"521053da7166ca435b9fb0f41222dac3ea0291f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/521053da7166ca435b9fb0f41222dac3ea0291f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/b2a4bb0e0c9bef64ba6a0ef2e97a788827d165ec","verification":{"payload":"tree 521053da7166ca435b9fb0f41222dac3ea0291f8\nparent 6201d06141b6435e865696bc132330ee1ee8f9e8\nauthor Paul Rastoin <45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com> 1783946346 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783946346 +0000\n\ndocs(apps): add Targeting System Fields page (#22856)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a docs page teaching app developers how to reference auto-created\n**system fields** (`createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `id`, …) from views and\nother entities, and makes the API it documents real by exporting\n`generateDefaultFieldUniversalIdentifier` from the SDK.\n\n## Why\n\nSystem fields are provisioned by the server, so they''re never declared\nwith `defineField()` and have no importable `universalIdentifier`\nconstant. Since 2.19 their universal identifier is derived\ndeterministically from the application id, the object id and the field\nname. Hardcoding an invented id fails sync with `INVALID_VIEW_DATA:\nField metadata not found` (this is exactly what broke the\ntwenty-partners `createdAt` view column).\n\nThe twenty-partners app already imports\n`generateDefaultFieldUniversalIdentifier` from `twenty-sdk/define`, but\nthe function was never exported from the SDK. This PR adds the export\nand documents the pattern.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **New page** `data/system-fields.mdx` — \"Targeting System Fields\":\n- Lists the 8 system fields (`id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`,\n`deletedAt`, `createdBy`, `updatedBy`, `position`, `searchVector`).\n- Explains the deterministic derivation and the sync error from\nhardcoding ids.\n- Documents `generateDefaultFieldUniversalIdentifier({\napplicationUniversalIdentifier, objectUniversalIdentifier, fieldName })`\nwith a full `defineView` example.\n- Contrasts with standard objects (use\n`STANDARD_OBJECT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS.<object>.fields.<field>.universalIdentifier`)\nand notes that `name` is a default, not system, field.\n- **SDK export** — new `generate-default-field-universal-identifier.ts`\nwrapping the existing `getFieldUniversalIdentifier` from\n`twenty-shared/application` (`name` → `fieldName`), exported from\n`define/index.ts`.\n- Registered the page in `docs.json` (Data group) and cross-linked it\nfrom the Views doc.\n\n## Notes\n\n`node_modules` isn''t installed in this environment, so `nx typecheck`\nwasn''t run. The wrapper is a signature-matched pass-through and the\n`twenty-shared/application` subpath + `getFieldUniversalIdentifier`\nbarrel export were both verified to exist.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_017B7VivHcqZYjn3ukestY9U)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22856?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions <github-actions@twenty.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVNxqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFHsQAGOUIAQmycQlv10X/oMblzZn\nm2Wo1r/usMreSxEfcMEQlw1oWzZFFhqUfifpwp9yEtefSeV1DUOsB16kOhrvLGbm\n2ZUXyxDLu/L+WMfUv+58zIAdz2mDAFoX6CcgoFyA9Tj/IGHhPQC67zP84m35MO7O\ngedWbINoAqWmQiYKcxVvdUg/PXjVSlMOBayrOuRkRlEHOUjQ/nY5OvZt69NKrWXa\nEmj2SNub6s0ACsNT40VwOX9JuDknIG37X3kznN+kk1XFD+K0jgiXrT0A2D9IItk0\nkEJQ4nvelFOyrw3YtyvGiQpKMF9gN2C1jnrUJKOPCnfNae7YFjY8JVIN/DwjnUxd\n7jMqeawFTFpxwxI3qeqAEGv1gk3p/bsBzVeQRZLCDm4bY0B8qLu02ElfeXgq3VG0\nvRRUqIWi2abOpalZ08ywfwuswrsoCT0dDRUlulhbOgvwJGzW9Ds09HNn6Ojol6SR\njUeI51k6n0neeQwhJyeAZZIWeWYvcqddwHbeW9Ua/qBQpTRQhtEgoFUYdtX4OvC2\ncZSzQGQweNF7xjbJ7OfBI5uXoEwz09bgcBFXLYrnE9vFMAjFSMo95YsSgtAIavBT\nFCx8wDApJoyOR2Zra8yRaiVw4B1Ff8vP/r7uZ1zSUlZPt5V6Er6UNcdvR+WhrDbN\nOA868yKSfruLIRzL0s8D\n=cOcO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:14:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/b2a4bb0e0c9bef64ba6a0ef2e97a788827d165ec","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKGIyYTRiYjBlMGM5YmVmNjRiYTZhMGVmMmU5N2E3ODg4MjdkMTY1ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/6201d06141b6435e865696bc132330ee1ee8f9e8","sha":"6201d06141b6435e865696bc132330ee1ee8f9e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/6201d06141b6435e865696bc132330ee1ee8f9e8"}],"sha":"b2a4bb0e0c9bef64ba6a0ef2e97a788827d165ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/b2a4bb0e0c9bef64ba6a0ef2e97a788827d165ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6399865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FelixMalfait","id":6399865,"login":"FelixMalfait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTk4NjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FelixMalfait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/6201d06141b6435e865696bc132330ee1ee8f9e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:30:38Z","email":"felix.malfait@gmail.com","name":"Félix Malfait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:30:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Preload Stripe.js before the onboarding payment step (#22858)\n\n## Context\n\nOn the plan-required onboarding step, the card form was slow to appear\nbecause Stripe.js is loaded lazily (`@stripe/stripe-js/pure`): the\nscript download only started once the payment page rendered, and the\nPaymentElement iframe could only boot after that.\n\n## What this does\n\n- Adds `usePreloadStripeForPlanRequiredStep`, called once from\n`OnboardingStepLayout` (the shared layout for the authenticated\nonboarding step routes), so Stripe.js is already loaded by the time the\nuser reaches the payment step. The hook only triggers when billing is\nenabled, the workspace has no subscription yet, and a publishable key is\nconfigured, so self-hosted instances still never contact Stripe.\n- Moves the memoized loader to\n`settings/billing/utils/getStripePromise.ts`, shared by\n`useStripePromise` and the preload hook.\n- Stops caching failed script loads: previously a rejected `loadStripe`\npromise stayed in the cache forever, which would have made a failed\npreload permanently break the payment form. Now a later call retries\n(stripe-js re-injects the script tag on retry).\n- Extracts the plan-required predicate into\n`onboarding/utils/getIsPlanRequired.ts`, now shared with\n`useSetNextOnboardingStatus`.\n\nThe in-app add-credit-card modal is intentionally left untouched: it has\nno preceding step to preload from.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `getStripePromise.test.ts`: dedup per publishable key, retry after a\nfailed load.\n- `usePreloadStripeForPlanRequiredStep.test.ts`: preloads when billing\nis enabled and no subscription exists; skips when billing is disabled, a\nsubscription exists, or the key is missing.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01NtUN99tHPZ6bPWwpYKMbpE)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22858?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"3c2524f63c35d37e356a7fb57612f763ceb348f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/3c2524f63c35d37e356a7fb57612f763ceb348f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/6201d06141b6435e865696bc132330ee1ee8f9e8","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c2524f63c35d37e356a7fb57612f763ceb348f5\nparent 9f5d17d1f063a40520499bbf8e908552092137f0\nauthor Félix Malfait <felix.malfait@gmail.com> 1783945838 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783945838 +0200\n\nPreload Stripe.js before the onboarding payment step (#22858)\n\n## Context\n\nOn the plan-required onboarding step, the card form was slow to appear\nbecause Stripe.js is loaded lazily (`@stripe/stripe-js/pure`): the\nscript download only started once the payment page rendered, and the\nPaymentElement iframe could only boot after that.\n\n## What this does\n\n- Adds `usePreloadStripeForPlanRequiredStep`, called once from\n`OnboardingStepLayout` (the shared layout for the authenticated\nonboarding step routes), so Stripe.js is already loaded by the time the\nuser reaches the payment step. The hook only triggers when billing is\nenabled, the workspace has no subscription yet, and a publishable key is\nconfigured, so self-hosted instances still never contact Stripe.\n- Moves the memoized loader to\n`settings/billing/utils/getStripePromise.ts`, shared by\n`useStripePromise` and the preload hook.\n- Stops caching failed script loads: previously a rejected `loadStripe`\npromise stayed in the cache forever, which would have made a failed\npreload permanently break the payment form. Now a later call retries\n(stripe-js re-injects the script tag on retry).\n- Extracts the plan-required predicate into\n`onboarding/utils/getIsPlanRequired.ts`, now shared with\n`useSetNextOnboardingStatus`.\n\nThe in-app add-credit-card modal is intentionally left untouched: it has\nno preceding step to preload from.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `getStripePromise.test.ts`: dedup per publishable key, retry after a\nfailed load.\n- `usePreloadStripeForPlanRequiredStep.test.ts`: preloads when billing\nis enabled and no subscription exists; skips when billing is disabled, a\nsubscription exists, or the key is missing.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01NtUN99tHPZ6bPWwpYKMbpE)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22858?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVNpuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP7kQAIUoAjKkh163gNWv69JHYAWU\nqjnTvgo0KPkZDurtOOWh0bPUL8+TvH1K9R0P3tszDOOjWDaSK+E3GMMnf4S/wmRk\nwuFCn6Pgu1kD6avwqJZ0/FBm/kbVVYiuBocJD+58T8EuOvA9r8tJ65jXzxOBoYj+\nHB+jjuxgm82a0/hMJStdqravAf9TFhM3HYoDa6MPN+T7P2itx1gjeQ72r1trGnp8\n7u7+/i2EuLSPn0O4PSad8oOn88Yz+3g1Fz3xJ8x7cRQmGabkAlkIbb7eBEm/RYeQ\nAqnffFT7iRA8+c/kiycZIUsSiRB1iCmc9oru3NTG5hG/mCEXjLlV8Yas2lFCkQnU\nKrPIcFO4HE1Ao+Fy6yHhwmSJ5gHCd8D1alwEyxjcyO7QdKHBs1HXEk/19FN+054w\nVNzvoZ1GgBFLcyTkXLSDjGMeVL8aPIRAzuyrsz9ZbHHl2/7mvahS2ypSthHqv4L+\n0VcCJx4tWWpLPeByAhuxGM+EHkMoYkUMGWXIMw8aZ0tLEOQdRZwDNGBz+zHOIkaQ\nRwhxxk9+kQTLPzZ00nl3WV5PAQg5gSxEZFjqaqBWM01eZchI0MUrH/gFEZgqmKpf\n6kI094yK2FMPAjvzTM1OJPdE9dzTGkVxxK8hTU4j8EgbNfbK2oB9yK/ZfE5nwKDa\n9YVi+DCpkIKC8nZ37Kbm\n=5xqQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:14:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/6201d06141b6435e865696bc132330ee1ee8f9e8","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKDYyMDFkMDYxNDFiNjQzNWU4NjU2OTZiYzEzMjMzMGVlMWVlOGY5ZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/9f5d17d1f063a40520499bbf8e908552092137f0","sha":"9f5d17d1f063a40520499bbf8e908552092137f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/9f5d17d1f063a40520499bbf8e908552092137f0"}],"sha":"6201d06141b6435e865696bc132330ee1ee8f9e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/6201d06141b6435e865696bc132330ee1ee8f9e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62795688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/neo773","id":62795688,"login":"neo773","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzk1Njg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/9f5d17d1f063a40520499bbf8e908552092137f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:28:21Z","email":"62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com","name":"neo773"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:28:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add receipt metrics and logs to connected account sync webhooks (#22853)\n\nWebhook deliveries from Google and Microsoft were invisible at the app\nlevel: successful notifications produced no logs and no metrics, so\nwebhook-triggered syncs could not be told apart from cron polling.\n\nAdd two counters, connected-account-sync-webhook/received/messaging and\n/received/calendar, mirroring the sync-job metric umbrellas, and log a\nline whenever a notification triggers a sync. Unmatched subscriptions\nkeep their existing warn logs.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22853?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"5360927f76cca0043a70f9b57854559876477c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/5360927f76cca0043a70f9b57854559876477c07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/9f5d17d1f063a40520499bbf8e908552092137f0","verification":{"payload":"tree 5360927f76cca0043a70f9b57854559876477c07\nparent 1b168ac1f7d466adf3be83b2676039e120d0db1c\nauthor neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com> 1783945701 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783945701 +0200\n\nAdd receipt metrics and logs to connected account sync webhooks (#22853)\n\nWebhook deliveries from Google and Microsoft were invisible at the app\nlevel: successful notifications produced no logs and no metrics, so\nwebhook-triggered syncs could not be told apart from cron polling.\n\nAdd two counters, connected-account-sync-webhook/received/messaging and\n/received/calendar, mirroring the sync-job metric umbrellas, and log a\nline whenever a notification triggers a sync. Unmatched subscriptions\nkeep their existing warn logs.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22853?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVNnlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGEAQAFjfJUcr6baYAXh3UZS33aGy\nj2gsYz76tBGyEtmmf7VK4DTcH8p2lWlMeSU+u8b+eTim269YJm0Qp0iMIxSsQf1V\nD6H6xfQmPSuSN9q0PZsAdFSwI9YR1ywv3E3NKOzXPIHWljP+24itfQ5LGU3OOOGZ\n/KI/UW1XztHp2hHdRX8xp63GO9SYj5lCzpAaY7GVTlkH8c77/+EURRk5fkxSPi8g\n/q+tSiE10jUosX71AlU28tMfK83bnzlezgeImrhozjJsOHyN3lFk1xVqayD/hcUn\nF+wu5qtBtfaLebQRQJRJsRIEbe1HXp1JczluJzynXrUBgEZX3yb4nl03VPBdCzOy\nws+JE7u7TIER+Ll5Q/08+iaJJ4mzs5n7/jfnrD/WU3JZncLj2yf+lnx6wQ1j0CTJ\n8cmPtbKTgpPrxAT62j80OWHF0dyDN6CdBiDemJJxxFf/5KvDL7CHFeE8PudWGW3x\n9LpETv3rtCaMzyZVxORQcOwiEd06iFjRK3EYqz8nT9J3SLUmRjLxnw2tmTOhyd5+\nIX9Gq0m+rKyI7x0hXSU+mMHWYqn67B0bScsieMKOI+0s3cvqRkhtVV/4wK9LxMee\nNd9vhgF2DjbovCl+N0M/yGSZVsoGBu0izZdMpQ559eS66pDcm55Q/MEy32uJh3y9\nKJJHM1UubBCYpM9Aiydw\n=1iN2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:14:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/9f5d17d1f063a40520499bbf8e908552092137f0","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKDlmNWQxN2QxZjA2M2E0MDUyMDQ5OWJiZjhlOTA4NTUyMDkyMTM3ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/1b168ac1f7d466adf3be83b2676039e120d0db1c","sha":"1b168ac1f7d466adf3be83b2676039e120d0db1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/1b168ac1f7d466adf3be83b2676039e120d0db1c"}],"sha":"9f5d17d1f063a40520499bbf8e908552092137f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/9f5d17d1f063a40520499bbf8e908552092137f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45004772?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prastoin","id":45004772,"login":"prastoin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA0Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/1b168ac1f7d466adf3be83b2676039e120d0db1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:20:28Z","email":"45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paul Rastoin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T12:20:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): gate workspaceDiscoverability behind upgrade decorator (#22818)\n\n## Context\n\nNeeds to be patched on 2.20, will craft a 2.19 equivalent with fallback\nasap ( be it won''t be merged unlike this one )\n\nFixes #22662. Follow-up to #22423, which introduced\n`workspaceDiscoverability`.\n\nA clean 2.18.x to 2.19 upgrade breaks on login with:\n\n```\nQueryFailedError: column workspaceDiscoverability does not exist\n```\n\n`workspaceDiscoverability` was added to `WorkspaceEntity` (in #22423) as\na plain, always-selected, non-nullable column, so any workspace query\n(including the auth-path `findAvailableWorkspacesByEmail` lookup) fails\nas soon as the ORM selects it, before the `2.19` upgrade command that\ncreates the column has run. Because the Docker entrypoint is fail-open,\nthe API starts even if the upgrade is delayed, and users hit this on\ntheir first login.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `@WasIntroducedInUpgrade` to `workspaceDiscoverability`,\nreferencing the existing `2.19.0` fast instance command that creates the\ncolumn. The upgrade-aware ORM then skips the column until the command\nhas actually added it, keeping login working during the upgrade.\n- Keep the GraphQL `@Field` non-nullable and add a\n`workspaceDiscoverability` `@ResolveField` that falls back to\n`WorkspaceDiscoverability.PUBLIC` while the column is hidden, so the\nresolver never returns `null` for the non-nullable field during the\nupgrade window.\n\nThis mirrors the existing pattern already applied to `FileEntity.status`\nand `FileEntity.applicationRegistrationId`, and the resolver-default\npattern already used for `fastModel` / `smartModel` / `logo`.\n\n## Cherry-pick\n\nThis fix needs to be cherry-picked onto both the **2.19** and **2.20**\nrelease branches, since affected instances are upgrading into those\nversions.\n\n## Test\n\n- `validate-upgrade-aware-entity-decorators` and\n`resolve-entity-shape-at-upgrade-cursor` unit tests pass (the referenced\nupgrade command name resolves correctly).\n- `upgrade-aware-repository.proxy` and\n`upgrade-aware-entity-metadata.adapter` specs pass.\n- `typecheck` and lint pass for `twenty-server` and `twenty-front`.\n- Regenerating the GraphQL schemas produces no diff (the field stays\nnon-nullable).","tree":{"sha":"23ee250ec85417c52a0067489d593b842fe46eed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/23ee250ec85417c52a0067489d593b842fe46eed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/1b168ac1f7d466adf3be83b2676039e120d0db1c","verification":{"payload":"tree 23ee250ec85417c52a0067489d593b842fe46eed\nparent 8e664112036f36fc14a0eb2873f3748df6a80c9f\nauthor Paul Rastoin <45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com> 1783945228 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783945228 +0000\n\nfix(server): gate workspaceDiscoverability behind upgrade decorator (#22818)\n\n## Context\n\nNeeds to be patched on 2.20, will craft a 2.19 equivalent with fallback\nasap ( be it won''t be merged unlike this one )\n\nFixes #22662. Follow-up to #22423, which introduced\n`workspaceDiscoverability`.\n\nA clean 2.18.x to 2.19 upgrade breaks on login with:\n\n```\nQueryFailedError: column workspaceDiscoverability does not exist\n```\n\n`workspaceDiscoverability` was added to `WorkspaceEntity` (in #22423) as\na plain, always-selected, non-nullable column, so any workspace query\n(including the auth-path `findAvailableWorkspacesByEmail` lookup) fails\nas soon as the ORM selects it, before the `2.19` upgrade command that\ncreates the column has run. Because the Docker entrypoint is fail-open,\nthe API starts even if the upgrade is delayed, and users hit this on\ntheir first login.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `@WasIntroducedInUpgrade` to `workspaceDiscoverability`,\nreferencing the existing `2.19.0` fast instance command that creates the\ncolumn. The upgrade-aware ORM then skips the column until the command\nhas actually added it, keeping login working during the upgrade.\n- Keep the GraphQL `@Field` non-nullable and add a\n`workspaceDiscoverability` `@ResolveField` that falls back to\n`WorkspaceDiscoverability.PUBLIC` while the column is hidden, so the\nresolver never returns `null` for the non-nullable field during the\nupgrade window.\n\nThis mirrors the existing pattern already applied to `FileEntity.status`\nand `FileEntity.applicationRegistrationId`, and the resolver-default\npattern already used for `fastModel` / `smartModel` / `logo`.\n\n## Cherry-pick\n\nThis fix needs to be cherry-picked onto both the **2.19** and **2.20**\nrelease branches, since affected instances are upgrading into those\nversions.\n\n## Test\n\n- `validate-upgrade-aware-entity-decorators` and\n`resolve-entity-shape-at-upgrade-cursor` unit tests pass (the referenced\nupgrade command name resolves correctly).\n- `upgrade-aware-repository.proxy` and\n`upgrade-aware-entity-metadata.adapter` specs pass.\n- `typecheck` and lint pass for `twenty-server` and `twenty-front`.\n- Regenerating the GraphQL schemas produces no diff (the field stays\nnon-nullable).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVNgMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5KgQAJR71ElQaLBCMU2tp5XhcoX4\nj6DoiPX2X6nTsFHS1sXce8PbIScnbBpwm2JxC1P6kDD/g63+CTi5338IJqAS+Z8s\nglr7SgJqcNqjBMBexKmHVmo2wdLPbkKRv54sk3fdaafJ0mgImYwhoalhlSVqZd8O\nAm0rwlMxp/Zx+SDKgDkQlZcpgEC2CZGjArD0mzYfNJ59bhdnRbsp5q4WEusgYy+c\nwLKkL7QhiGSGn9Phb8V05kg4flEuY5ivvHkFKMJdf2OYHXmf4G8owhh/5Em8Mp3G\nKZspb2gEpYXRA9KntVEVu7WU0PHU5N3Dxql/CYsMjrtd5/moDQrhFWr+TblKXYnI\nTgMAeJy1Is2fpL2TdwZHLQyFQF2mjUmZdCr4JuLyvROCn5mSM42q9+aoWDCiKNzP\n91ppLFxyn1x+