m/neo773","id":62795688,"login":"neo773","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzk1Njg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neo773","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/b0dc637dbd3ea8744764557afd84399a341f7c86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:28:34Z","email":"62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com","name":"neo773"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T18:28:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Throw proper error on duplicate emailing domain (#22790)\n\nAdding an emailing domain that already exists blew up with a raw\nQueryFailedError and the client just saw a generic \"An error occurred\".\nThe unique index on domain is global, so the workspace-scoped existence\ncheck never caught rows owned by another workspace.\n\nNow the check is unscoped and throws an EmailingDomainException mapped\nto CONFLICT with a proper user-facing message, in both the\ncreateEmailingDomain mutation and the email group channel flow. Also\ndropped the hardcoded catch-all snackbar on the new channel page so\nserver messages actually reach the user.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22790?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"6c882c981475961b7bad92cf0cc963b406930062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/6c882c981475961b7bad92cf0cc963b406930062"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/b0dc637dbd3ea8744764557afd84399a341f7c86","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c882c981475961b7bad92cf0cc963b406930062\nparent cb95410a51f7de99415b347a9d54d3e33e1a4982\nauthor neo773 <62795688+neo773@users.noreply.github.com> 1783708114 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783708114 +0200\n\nThrow proper error on duplicate emailing domain (#22790)\n\nAdding an emailing domain that already exists blew up with a raw\nQueryFailedError and the client just saw a generic \"An error occurred\".\nThe unique index on domain is global, so the workspace-scoped existence\ncheck never caught rows owned by another workspace.\n\nNow the check is unscoped and throws an EmailingDomainException mapped\nto CONFLICT with a proper user-facing message, in both the\ncreateEmailingDomain mutation and the email group channel flow. Also\ndropped the hardcoded catch-all snackbar on the new channel page so\nserver messages actually reach the user.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22790?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJ