ist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/ab9e6f30b83fa9c0d9c238f6d5f0321a982db328","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKGFiOWU2ZjMwYjgzZmE5YzBkOWMyMzhmNmQ1ZjAzMjFhOTgyZGIzMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/7f8a1da27a9f37c01c24656c21348b32ea7d7cc6","sha":"7f8a1da27a9f37c01c24656c21348b32ea7d7cc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/7f8a1da27a9f37c01c24656c21348b32ea7d7cc6"}],"sha":"ab9e6f30b83fa9c0d9c238f6d5f0321a982db328","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/ab9e6f30b83fa9c0d9c238f6d5f0321a982db328"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29927851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/martmull","id":29927851,"login":"martmull","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/7f8a1da27a9f37c01c24656c21348b32ea7d7cc6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:26:07Z","email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:26:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix Cloudflare rate limiting during last-contact backfill (#22811)\n\n## Context\n\nUpgrading `twenty-last-contact` on a production workspace failed with a\nCloudflare error 1015 (\"You are being rate limited\"). The\n`backfill-last-contact` post-install function runs on every version\nupgrade and fired 20 concurrent update mutations per batch with no pause\nbetween batches, on top of paginated full-collection reads. On a\nworkspace with real email/calendar history that burst trips Cloudflare''s\nrate limit, and since the client SDK throws on any non-2xx response, a\nsingle 429 killed the whole install/upgrade hook mid-backfill.\n\n## Changes\n\n- New `executeWithRetry` util: retries rate-limit (429 / Cloudflare\n1015) and transient gateway/network errors (502/503/504, timeouts,\nconnection resets) with exponential backoff and jitter, capped at 5\nattempts. Honors a `retry_after` hint when present in the response body.\nNon-retryable errors still throw immediately.\n- All backfill queries and mutations are wrapped with it.\n- Update batch concurrency reduced from 20 to 10 to keep bursts under\nthe rate limit in the first place.\n- Bumped app version to 1.1.1 with a changelog entry.\n\n## Test\n\n- Added unit tests for `executeWithRetry` (success passthrough,\nretry-then-succeed, non-retryable passthrough, retry exhaustion,\n`retry_after` handling).\n- `yarn test:unit` (28 passed), `yarn typecheck`, `yarn lint` all green\nin the app package.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01AtnkEfbpFhLp5qCJbSmZpE)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22811?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"effc9ef08489c062396d3d7f9f432da5b83deb16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/effc9ef08489c062396d3d7f9f432da5b83deb16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/7f8a1da27a9f37c01c24656c21348b32ea7d7cc6","verification":{"payload":"tree effc9ef08489c062396d3d7f9f432da5b83deb16\nparent 7861ada5898e6bb062cf14b76380ec7a35b76f87\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1783689967 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783689967 +0200\n\nFix Cloudflare rate limiting during last-contact backfill (#22811)\n\n## Context\n\nUpgrading `twenty-last-contact` on a production workspace failed with a\nCloudflare error 1015 (\"You are being rate limited\"). The\n`backfill-last-contact` post-install function runs on every version\nupgrade and fired 20 concurrent update mutations per batch with no pause\nbetween batches, on top of paginated full-collection reads. On a\nworkspace with real email/calendar history that burst trips Cloudflare''s\nrate limit, and since the client SDK throws on any non-2xx response, a\nsingle 429 killed the whole install/upgrade hook mid-backfill.\n\n## Changes\n\n- New `executeWithRetry` util: retries rate-limit (429 / Cloudflare\n1015) and transient gateway/network errors (502/503/504, timeouts,\nconnection resets) with exponential backoff and jitter, capped at 5\nattempts. Honors a `retry_after` hint when present in the response body.\nNon-retryable errors still throw immediately.\n- All backfill queries and mutations are wrapped with it.\n- Update batch concurrency reduced from 20 to 10 to keep bursts under\nthe rate limit in the first place.\n- Bumped app version to 1.1.1 with a changelog entry.\n\n## Test\n\n- Added unit tests for `executeWithRetry` (success passthrough,\nretry-then-succeed, non-retryable passthrough, retry exhaustion,\n`retry_after` handling).\n- `yarn test:unit` (28 passed), `yarn typecheck`, `yarn lint` all green\nin the app package.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01AtnkEfbpFhLp5qCJbSmZpE)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22811?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUPLvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3IgQAKD5OoZD6pdEijhSjNkH/Uh0\nk5hz4E9tYa4mfIS7L7365pFt4A1jI3oI4sCQScQpQGj1IWHijw2Kgl/xuWuQvPCI\n8z2uHGpXDTFb/Wjv1DCJMM49iVfyFJB5+BtyWgTKi85FkCM2+d9EVL/ObBEkqEP8\nDQ0a9GEqcSjTkbgyKwRC/wBHm1e9zQEW0vX48HAZ7pL+GH4rYidL3Z/UZ0Q+/Msv\niMoill9i+S2LDE+egcMImcvBeSzLmjTUc3Wbw1VbS03fVXQBWwkYs76BzGpCFZte\nU+aImHf8w9SvNEDnrbZRLXyIpPLA/XFUt4eOEmoIb44JA0L9h/D84DxYkyq7Gr3N\nr/2Vsa9Oj85KVPicLMBfNitgHQ+eY5qf68I7sdTKOfTV88JKsUZZ0n4pehIt8k8W\nrpvfeRtgUZfRNOPdtFgmL/KDTtt5KR/HeimO+YUNsDH1uyC1uGpRZNBp9a3Avo3Y\ndvp88mmSP+v0yeAJ6Cs5wguol/oHwzSm3GOKtUT+SC3+wLXwloGNs54IRDVO1i6L\nx9Xw0h9gfIcYUgzpNMePLC2