_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/945724e016d05744e73959c7dca80ff60efc9aba","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKDk0NTcyNGUwMTZkMDU3NDRlNzM5NTljN2RjYTgwZmY2MGVmYzlhYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/666ceb41d5f2c7e9225cfc934769a8aff1bd30a3","sha":"666ceb41d5f2c7e9225cfc934769a8aff1bd30a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/666ceb41d5f2c7e9225cfc934769a8aff1bd30a3"}],"sha":"945724e016d05744e73959c7dca80ff60efc9aba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/945724e016d05744e73959c7dca80ff60efc9aba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/666ceb41d5f2c7e9225cfc934769a8aff1bd30a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:11:46Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:11:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix SDK plan on non installed apps (#22805)\n\n# Context\n\n`yarn twenty plan` fails when the app has never been installed in the\ntarget workspace:\n\n```\nSync failed with error: Application \"f5ce204f-...\" is not installed in workspace \"10f39a9d-...\". Install it first.\nHint: run `yarn twenty dev --once` to register the app in this workspace, then retry.\n```\n\nThis forces developers to apply before they can plan, which defeats the\npurpose of `plan`. Planning a not-yet-installed app is well defined: the\nfrom-state is empty, so the plan is simply \"create everything\".\n\n## Why it failed\n\nThe dry-run sync required the application row to exist in two places:\n\n1. `ApplicationSyncService.synchronizeFromManifest` threw\n`APP_NOT_INSTALLED` when the app row was missing, because the dry-run\nneeds an owner `FlatApplication` to anchor the from → to metadata diff.\n2.\n`WorkspaceMigrationFlatEntityMapsService.computeAllInvolvedApplicationIds`\nthrew when the owner app id was absent from `flatApplicationMaps`, even\nthough the only hard dependency of a build is the twenty standard\napplication.\n\n`apply` never hit this because it registers the app row as a side effect\nbefore syncing (and even swallows this exact error on its pre-apply\nplan).\n\n# What this PR does\n\nKeeps `plan` strictly read-only, no registration or app row is created:\n\n- **`application-sync.service.ts`**: on dry-run, resolve the owner to\nthe installed application when it exists (unchanged behavior), otherwise\nbuild a virtual, non-persisted `FlatApplication` from the manifest. Its\nfreshly generated id matches no existing metadata, so the from-state\nslice resolves to empty and every manifest entity shows up as a create.\n- **`workspace-migration-flat-entity-maps.service.ts`**: relax the guard\nso only the twenty standard application is required. A missing owner app\njust contributes an empty from-slice instead of throwing. Installed apps\ntake the exact same path as before (`applicationId` defined → identical\nbehavior).","tree":{"sha":"97c98820c281e5ebd55f2d9b6f719b69f5ba5af1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/97c98820c281e5ebd55f2d9b6f719b69f5ba5af1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/666ceb41d5f2c7e9225cfc934769a8aff1bd30a3","verification":{"payload":"tree 97c98820c281e5ebd55f2d9b6f719b69f5ba5af1\nparent 60f5964c64f36667ccea70126898969756b17593\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1783689106 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783689106 +0200\n\nFix SDK plan on non installed apps (#22805)\n\n# Context\n\n`yarn twenty plan` fails when the app has never been installed in the\ntarget workspace:\n\n```\nSync failed with error: Application \"f5ce204f-...\" is not installed in workspace \"10f39a9d-...\". Install it first.\nHint: run `yarn twenty dev --once` to register the app in this workspace, then retry.\n```\n\nThis forces developers to apply before they can plan, which defeats the\npurpose of `plan`. Planning a not-yet-installed app is well defined: the\nfrom-state is empty, so the plan is simply \"create everything\".\n\n## Why it failed\n\nThe dry-run sync required the application row to exist in two places:\n\n1. `ApplicationSyncService.synchronizeFromManifest` threw\n`APP_NOT_INSTALLED` when the app row was missing, because the dry-run\nneeds an owner `FlatApplication` to anchor the from → to metadata diff.\n2.\n`WorkspaceMigrationFlatEntityMapsService.computeAllInvolvedApplicationIds`\nthrew when the owner app id was absent from `flatApplicationMaps`, even\nthough the only hard dependency of a build is the twenty standard\napplication.\n\n`apply` never hit this because it registers the app row as a side effect\nbefore syncing (and even swallows this exact error on its pre-apply\nplan).\n\n# What this PR does\n\nKeeps `plan` strictly read-only, no registration or app row is created:\n\n- **`application-sync.service.ts`**: on dry-run, resolve the owner to\nthe installed application when it exists (unchanged behavior), otherwise\nbuild a virtual, non-persisted `FlatApplication` from the manifest. Its\nfreshly generated id matches no existing metadata, so the from-state\nslice resolves to empty and every manifest entity shows up as a create.\n- **`workspace-migration-flat-entity-maps.service.ts`**: relax the guard\nso only the twenty standard application is required. A missing owner app\njust contributes an empty from-slice instead of throwing. Installed apps\ntake the exact same path as before (`applicationId` defined → identical\nbehavior).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUO+SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVX0QAHXSUrmOMA5Bo0QkZhJxQ812\ndkkBirLBay+bzJh1qZ4Ozy//fthl7PslKrzVTSzVqs/F51DS4u0XMMIjbKgF7+p8\nj0/TnCDlWeBTf2WhpLQT8zHRiAVFkBZphgBV5DHiTsbRGjPF0sbxe2mavLJpPQ6t\nT23hPJhdVV+ETu6HuQxd3htUiOz8wD843nbhV9wiVpgeJNHujBw2GWhrS1hAs54s\nsBb+N2T2tjWcWWT/5cTqKv6X33fpYStB4ODNUOqfCRrZ0u6HqEdGV+K5Oo3HaoAN\njVXluaE9CX4PNLCytvJiIlIlei5oaRDjTqkVnusYkjnB4X4c8Fyg7Tc9yyofUjkr\nl4w2eLDkfkD8vyRNWjcP1IFMdnhZgk5eCcVgVZCzEVf1FiI/I+62LzA4fq3ZGGOB\n1Wb4g/fJKXfu/p/Njg0FVjowzDstHN4M3JnVUVjhRP+uz4889vLViwxLvIb8wFkN\nFfhaFEEePAaA7RZbN/UHKqy5BvLZj+EWdJZLgcc2/qPCRBZdMBgzR34ITaOTKac9\njA3gYvCCLsncuvoeTkUv01d3TjpKw1ZlXn0r+b/jqMIseyXbRYrcwt+tY3wRBnUu\n4rmiVbJTZg229JM5Jtx0MFtBnMVFznTdSN26CoxgsJ5o+mBGlMmSn5V7LKApovEi\n5J61srnzsqzuz+Tip1Gd\n=/DEp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:14:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/666ceb41d5f2c7e9225cfc934769a8aff1bd30a3","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKDY2NmNlYjQxZDVmMmM3ZTkyMjVjZmM5MzQ3NjlhOGFmZjFiZDMwYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/60f5964c64f36667ccea70126898969756b17593","sha":"60f5964c64f36667ccea70126898969756b17593","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/60f5964c64f36667ccea70126898969756b17593"}],"sha":"666ceb41d5f2c7e9225cfc934769a8aff1bd30a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/666ceb41d5f2c7e9225cfc934769a8aff1bd30a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/60f5964c64f36667ccea70126898969756b17593/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:10:30Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-10T13:10:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Run front components in a sandboxed opaque-origin iframe (#22588)\n\nFront components run untrusted third-party React in a Web Worker. That\nworker previously shared the host origin, so it could reach\norigin-scoped storage (the metadata-store IndexedDB, the\n`twenty-sign-out` BroadcastChannel), cookies, and same-origin resources.\n\nThis runs the worker inside a `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` (no\n`allow-same-origin`) iframe, giving it an opaque origin where the\nbrowser denies localStorage, cookies, IndexedDB, and BroadcastChannel\noutright. The worker is kept inside the iframe (rather than a bare\niframe) so untrusted code always runs off the main thread; the\nremote-dom render path is unchanged.\n\n- **Transport:** host ↔ iframe ↔ worker over a re-transferred\n`MessagePort` (`ThreadMessagePort`); a small bootstrap script is inlined\ninto the iframe via `srcdoc` (bundled at build time by a prebuild step)\nand relays the port to the worker it spawns. Messages across the\nboundary use a typed discriminated union with a single parse/guard.\n- **Network:** under the opaque origin, direct fetches to the Twenty API\nwould be `Origin: null`, so the component source and SDK modules are\nfetched through an allowlisted, credential-omitting `hostFetch` bridge\nand blobbed inside the worker. The allowlist is single-sourced on the\nhost (http(s) origins only) and carried in the render context. The\nbridge is mandatory (rendering fails closed if it is missing), refuses\nredirects except for GET/HEAD to the known file-storage URLs, and caps\nresponse body size.\n- **SDK loading:** SDK client modules now load inside the worker through\nthe bridge, replacing the host-side SDK-blob state/effect/provider with\na pure `getSdkClientUrls` URL builder.\n- **Isolation tests:** a unit test locks the sandbox attribute\n(`allow-scripts`, never `allow-same-origin`); a browser test asserts the\nworker actually gets an opaque origin with storage denied, probing\ncookies by writing one rather than reading an empty jar.\n\nAlso adds a \"List Companies\" seed front component that queries workspace\ndata via the SDK client (exercising the bridge end-to-end),\nsingle-sources the command-menu confirmation-modal result event name and\ndetail type in `twenty-shared` (previously a hand-synced duplicate), and\ndecomposes the renderer (bridge, sandbox, worker orchestration) into\nsmall single-purpose utils with unit tests.\n\n## How it works\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    participant Host as Host window (twenty-front · host origin)\n    participant Frame as Sandboxed iframe (allow-scripts · opaque origin)\n    participant Worker as Worker (untrusted component · opaque origin)\n    participant API as Twenty API (host origin)\n\n    rect rgb(238,242,248)\n    Note over Host,Worker: 1 — Boot handshake\n    Host->>Frame: create iframe sandbox=\"allow-scripts\", srcdoc = inlined bootstrap script\n    Host->>Host: MessageChannel + ThreadMessagePort(port1)<br/>exports = host API + hostFetch\n    Frame-->>Host: READY\n    Host->>Frame: INIT + transfer port2\n    Frame->>Worker: spawn inlined Worker + re-transfer port2\n    Worker->>Worker: ThreadMessagePort(port)<br/>exports = render / updateContext\n    Note over Host,Worker: Port now entangles Host ↔ Worker directly\n    end\n\n    rect rgb(246,240,248)\n    Note over Host,Worker: 2 — Render\n    Host->>Worker: render(connection, { componentUrl, sdkClientUrls, hostFetchOrigins, token })\n    Worker->>Worker: override globalThis.fetch<br/>(Twenty origins → hostFetch)\n    end\n\n    rect rgb(248,244,238)\n    Note over Worker,API: 3 — Network via hostFetch bridge (opaque Origin:null cannot reach the API directly)\n    Worker->>Host: hostFetch(componentUrl, Bearer)\n    Host->>Host: origin allowlist + credentials:''omit''\n    Host->>API: fetch(componentUrl)\n    API-->>Host: source\n    Host-->>Worker: { status, headers, body }\n    Worker->>Host: hostFetch(sdkClientUrls.core / .metadata)\n    Host-->>Worker: SDK module sources\n    Worker->>Worker: blob each source in its own opaque origin → import() → run untrusted React\n    end\n\n    rect rgb(238,248,242)\n    Note over Worker,Host: 4 — Render mirror\n    Worker->>Host: remote-dom mutations (RemoteConnection)\n    Host->>Host: RemoteReceiver → RemoteRootRenderer → host DOM\n    end\n\n    Note over Worker: Opaque origin ⇒ browser denies localStorage,<br/>cookies, IndexedDB, BroadcastChannel\n```","tree":{"sha":"aab96ceb0af2180984ba35ce2c15d47194c30e0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/aab96ceb0af2180984ba35ce2c15d47194c30e0b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/60f5964c64f36667ccea70126898969756b17593","verification":{"payload":"tree aab96ceb0af2180984ba35ce2c15d47194c30e0b\nparent 95b672e61e7e08ff353f41902fac1c1431228ba0\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1783689030 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783689030 +0000\n\nRun front components in a sandboxed opaque-origin iframe (#22588)\n\nFront components run untrusted third-party React in a Web Worker. That\nworker previously shared the host origin, so it could reach\norigin-scoped storage (the metadata-store IndexedDB, the\n`twenty-sign-out` BroadcastChannel), cookies, and same-origin resources.\n\nThis runs the worker inside a `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` (no\n`allow-same-origin`) iframe, giving it an opaque origin where the\nbrowser denies localStorage, cookies, IndexedDB, and BroadcastChannel\noutright. The worker is kept inside the iframe (rather than a bare\niframe) so untrusted code always runs off the main thread; the\nremote-dom render path is unchanged.\n\n- **Transport:** host ↔ iframe ↔ worker over a re-transferred\n`MessagePort` (`ThreadMessagePort`); a small bootstrap script is inlined\ninto the iframe via `srcdoc` (bundled at build time by a prebuild step)\nand relays the port to the worker it spawns. Messages across the\nboundary use a typed discriminated union with a single parse/guard.\n- **Network:** under the opaque origin, direct fetches to the Twenty API\nwould be `Origin: null`, so the component source and SDK modules are\nfetched through an allowlisted, credential-omitting `hostFetch` bridge\nand blobbed inside the worker. The allowlist is single-sourced on the\nhost (http(s) origins only) and carried in the render context. The\nbridge is mandatory (rendering fails closed if it is missing), refuses\nredirects except for GET/HEAD to the known file-storage URLs, and caps\nresponse body size.\n- **SDK loading:** SDK client modules now load inside the worker through\nthe bridge, replacing the host-side SDK-blob state/effect/provider with\na pure `getSdkClientUrls` URL builder.\n- **Isolation tests:** a unit test locks the sandbox attribute\n(`allow-scripts`, never `allow-same-origin`); a browser test asserts the\nworker actually gets an opaque origin with storage denied, probing\ncookies by writing one rather than reading an empty jar.\n\nAlso adds a \"List Companies\" seed front component that queries workspace\ndata via the SDK client (exercising the bridge end-to-end),\nsingle-sources the command-menu confirmation-modal result event name and\ndetail type in `twenty-shared` (previously a hand-synced duplicate), and\ndecomposes the renderer (bridge, sandbox, worker orchestration) into\nsmall single-purpose utils with unit tests.\n\n## How it works\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    participant Host as Host window (twenty-front · host origin)\n    participant Frame as Sandboxed iframe (allow-scripts · opaque origin)\n    participant Worker as Worker (untrusted component · opaque origin)\n    participant API as Twenty API (host origin)\n\n    rect rgb(238,242,248)\n    Note over Host,Worker: 1 — Boot handshake\n    Host->>Frame: create iframe sandbox=\"allow-scripts\", srcdoc = inlined bootstrap script\n    Host->>Host: MessageChannel + ThreadMessagePort(port1)<br/>exports = host API + hostFetch\n    Frame-->>Host: READY\n    Host->>Frame: INIT + transfer port2\n    Frame->>Worker: spawn inlined Worker + re-transfer port2\n    Worker->>Worker: ThreadMessagePort(port)<br/>exports = render / updateContext\n    Note over Host,Worker: Port now entangles Host ↔ Worker directly\n    end\n\n    rect rgb(246,240,248)\n    Note over Host,Worker: 2 — Render\n    Host->>Worker: render(connection, { componentUrl, sdkClientUrls, hostFetchOrigins, token })\n    Worker->>Worker: override globalThis.fetch<br/>(Twenty origins → hostFetch)\n    end\n\n    rect rgb(248,244,238)\n    Note over Worker,API: 3 — Network via hostFetch bridge (opaque Origin:null cannot reach the API directly)\n    Worker->>Host: hostFetch(componentUrl, Bearer)\n    Host->>Host: origin allowlist + credentials:''omit''\n    Host->>API: fetch(componentUrl)\n    API-->>Host: source\n    Host-->>Worker: { status, headers, body }\n    Worker->>Host: hostFetch(sdkClientUrls.core / .metadata)\n    Host-->>Worker: SDK module sources\n    Worker->>Worker: blob each source in its own opaque origin → import() → run untrusted React\n    end\n\n    rect rgb(238,248,242)\n    Note over Worker,Host: 4 — Render mirror\n    Worker->>Host: remote-dom mutations (RemoteConnection)\n    Host->>Host: RemoteReceiver → RemoteRootRenderer → host DOM\n    end\n\n    Note over Worker: Opaque origin ⇒ browser denies localStorage,<br/>cookies, IndexedDB, BroadcastChannel\n```","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUO9GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmyIQABiaZcc/UYxfg9JQ7e4Xqzet\net5w5TV8kc5DvktQN3uOTFcrm0cutq6563uTTMJTtMERRswFqtO732E+HJRGLwRQ\nJSCbsnE+Foyg8lmN9JoFUn+aL1qHDCDLjM45aiPDca0na05PIByrkD7rdbVraVym\njrvQkV/Xo4mIuU8duY1iDd8W7/9NZGraWW/zzKSkD/ZoAxsj2SYkooZdsDnyMiCD\nZ+2Jc+7v6ctoCBpAbcpOoixsyhHSkhGsJ/nFJfF9p9Dqk9L7S8F/FgqaRDFqFurs\n6+Q9jt8aD/aQR0RZZ5JJj4wKFRNH+tsZvB0qpXQxlYzODbuLZfTFe5yEz54i6MDc\nDtWicWAQdx8wI7EI6VZnDL0t1dvMxiZlwzGMHOPFKUNz5Awz0FKlX1cqOVbjIALq\nFWLjwqmEx1FBVRDS1EGRbsUIadipc8F16fvprWMnTRUYqT9eCKetOYh4/BiOS4o0\nfIMozTJSoiTVxJmT3V1Zyj3iUoNSQXKVTfvbr8RyS3Geg2w3mnuTKq+kEsJyeMFV\nC8fpdYcp4g5TSaRS4A3bGV5nKMcRdvVKH7Mw1OA+JvEC6QUg9rxZAnD7Ts9tnz4J\nwJ/WEjNpTfGHbTuNeqjIInlL0pmJiPPmTOT5dk4w1Yc1TKOrOAi5IN5eWRwgS7Bg\nJynBPHwgVG6j727Xbcwj\n=rlJg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:14:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flo