NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/b47e64c9e3b3c5da28d3f278942332e33849f5b2","sha":"b47e64c9e3b3c5da28d3f278942332e33849f5b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/b47e64c9e3b3c5da28d3f278942332e33849f5b2"}],"sha":"60fd322b49174fbc8624b5a0b91ab879765a2966","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/60fd322b49174fbc8624b5a0b91ab879765a2966"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11599358?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rashad","id":11599358,"login":"rashad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTk5MzU4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rashad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/b47e64c9e3b3c5da28d3f278942332e33849f5b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:56:52Z","email":"11599358+rashad@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Rashad Karanouh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:56:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: surface the self-serve partner marketplace on high-intent pages (#22719)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds partner-marketplace CTAs to four high-intent docs pages (enterprise\n+ migration), routing readers to the **self-serve** partner directory\n(`twenty.com/partners/list`) while keeping `contact@twenty.com` as a\nsecondary option. This upgrades pages that previously only offered the\nold \"email us to be matched\" path (or no partner path at all).\n\nRendered with Mintlify-native components — `<Tip>` callouts, plus a\n`<CardGroup>` on the Implementation Services page. No new snippet; no\n`docs.json`, navigation, or translation (`l/`) changes.\n\n## Pages changed — screenshots (one per page)\n\n> Preview locally with `npx nx run twenty-docs:dev` (localhost:3000), or\nuse the Mintlify PR preview once it posts on this PR. Paths below are\nunder `docs.twenty.com`.\n\n### 1. `/user-guide/permissions-access/capabilities/sso-configuration`\n`<Tip>` callout → *Find a certified Twenty partner* (Solutioning),\n`contact@twenty.com` as a secondary aside.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"712\" height=\"616\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-09 at 12 14 05\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6521634-7783-466f-bfae-a4a49f64d941\"\n/>\n\n\n### 2.\n`/user-guide/data-migration/how-tos/migrating-from-self-hosted-to-cloud`\n`<Tip>` callout → *Get a certified Twenty partner* (Hosting), contact\nfallback.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"665\" height=\"193\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-09 at 12 14 23\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/30ecb4d2-fb7e-4e0f-9355-491713290f90\"\n/>\n\n\n### 3. `/user-guide/data-migration/how-tos/migrating-from-other-crms`\n`<Tip>` callout → **Done for you** (partner) vs **Onboarding pack**\n(Twenty team).\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"659\" height=\"273\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-09 at 12 14 35\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9cc5bb3e-c8be-4734-9e03-dc5b536eeeb7\"\n/>\n\n\n### 4.\n`/user-guide/getting-started/capabilities/implementation-services`\n`<CardGroup>` → **Browse certified partners** / **Get matched by\nTwenty**.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"706\" height=\"766\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-09 at 12 14 47\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01b69197-0f47-46fe-a40e-92c11286827e\"\n/>\n\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- Links deep-link the directory via `?categories=<scope>` (verified\nlive) and carry a `?ref=docs-*` tag.\n- **Attribution caveat:** twenty.com''s analytics (Cloudflare Web\nAnalytics) is path-based, so `?ref=` is not measurable yet.\n- `contact@twenty.com` intentionally kept as a secondary option.\n- `mintlify validate` passes.\n\nOpened as a draft.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22719?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"42376bf091bfd9e170c8ab16092052b1fe8c9278","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/42376bf091bfd9e170c8ab16092052b1fe8c9278"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/b47e64c9e3b3c5da28d3f278942332e33849f5b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 42376bf091bfd9e170c8ab16092052b1fe8c9278\nparent f06ba08b162590f8c1bf89410723f8523f9b0484\nauthor Rashad Karanouh <11599358+rashad@users.noreply.github.com> 1783609012 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783609012 +0200\n\ndocs: surface the self-serve partner marketplace on high-intent pages (#22719)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds partner-marketplace CTAs to four high-intent docs pages (enterprise\n+ migration), routing readers to the **self-serve** partner directory\n(`twenty.com/partners/list`) while keeping `contact@twenty.com` as a\nsecondary option. This upgrades pages that previously only offered the\nold \"email us to be matched\" path (or no partner path at all).\n\nRendered with Mintlify-native components — `<Tip>` callouts, plus a\n`<CardGroup>` on the Implementation Services page. No new snippet; no\n`docs.json`, navigation, or translation (`l/`) changes.\n\n## Pages changed — screenshots (one per page)\n\n> Preview locally with `npx nx run twenty-docs:dev` (localhost:3000), or\nuse the Mintlify PR preview once it posts on this PR. Paths below are\nunder `docs.twenty.com`.\n\n### 1. `/user-guide/permissions-access/capabilities/sso-configuration`\n`<Tip>` callout → *Find a certified Twenty partner* (Solutioning),\n`contact@twenty.com` as a secondary aside.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"712\" height=\"616\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-09 at 12 14 05\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6521634-7783-466f-bfae-a4a49f64d941\"\n/>\n\n\n### 2.\n`/user-guide/data-migration/how-tos/migrating-from-self-hosted-to-cloud`\n`<Tip>` callout → *Get a certified Twenty partner* (Hosting), contact\nfallback.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"665\" height=\"193\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-09 at 12 14 23\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/30ecb4d2-fb7e-4e0f-9355-491713290f90\"\n/>\n\n\n### 3. `/user-guide/data-migration/how-tos/migrating-from-other-crms`\n`<Tip>` callout → **Done for you** (partner) vs **Onboarding pack**\n(Twenty team).\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"659\" height=\"273\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-09 at 12 14 35\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9cc5bb3e-c8be-4734-9e03-dc5b536eeeb7\"\n/>\n\n\n### 4.\n`/user-guide/getting-started/capabilities/implementation-services`\n`<CardGroup>` → **Browse certified partners** / **Get matched by\nTwenty**.\n\n_screenshot:_\n<img width=\"706\" height=\"766\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-09 at 12 14 47\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01b69197-0f47-46fe-a40e-92c11286827e\"\n/>\n\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- Links deep-link the directory via `?categories=<scope>` (verified\nlive) and carry a `?ref=docs-*` tag.\n- **Attribution caveat:** twenty.com''s analytics (Cloudflare Web\nAnalytics) is path-based, so `?ref=` is not measurable yet.\n- `contact@twenty.com` intentionally kept as a secondary option.\n- `mintlify validate` passes.\n\nOpened as a draft.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22719?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT7a0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOl0QAH8NV7FAObT9xh5EtufxfDBT\n4l/mAsYAoR/nPOzYMpsSQJ9oTF8a3tGMo7w9DVTKLX9Drhjlw4X1AyomoDaHl52B\nJTvX0gywMbICIWMMzx00JQgS2fsA/X3GhWo+OKqMQ6Dx1V9G/OOmJkMBv7Mblwno\nkcivVhRBnLY8framnMRBC5yVJy6t8vpG4JZps5KlZkQMFKPjEmKNwHuceDxFKMnx\nFHiH+e5v4dGFVbVGUzxU04+VT01olXakcfV94wQ307pM31nUoSWrq//PgZVF84yq\nlXhSIxT94jtNYsz2w/3vtfSTDwxUDiyNIxGEZfBOvakPuleu1/yWpZDrM51Hubxj\ndDkWDoILO9JW4zOwM8lOl8KiFOhfylDSZWSuwONOqqtmiSTeXWLBq621/6oBeDpr\nr6kjTYe/nAOKvK4iOszTKpzYVqzOr8ksAoi5liY6h/BKS3ukLQjvOnEXH9twsRFw\nBVsZDPxWuqDBgyfNQTfEc5uJlgAaw9sOr9l5Vko/e0zEAHTYIzAnAscaALCh8Lbd\nnNsSaJcr9duVss9HvrJXDz9W9f3h/h7eLiuZKR0Qf4rE8Th2z3IwrPF/H/0a7CSI\nSCfycZSCXpvRGvPBJDoD5QgKT4FqwBH0H/Z1GoTmicjjDs7lCA7q4jmMaSkEKsFP\nXSOe5UZMwNTV9+M0d3Gu\n=+qfX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:14:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/b47e64c9e3b3c5da28d3f278942332e33849f5b2","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKGI0N2U2NGM5ZTNiM2M1ZGEyOGQzZjI3ODk0MjMzMmUzMzg0OWY1YjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/f06ba08b162590f8c1bf89410723f8523f9b0484","sha":"f06ba08b162590f8c1bf89410723f8523f9b0484","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/f06ba08b162590f8c1bf89410723f8523f9b0484"}],"sha":"b47e64c9e3b3c5da28d3f278942332e33849f5b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/b47e64c9e3b3c5da28d3f278942332e33849f5b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/f06ba08b162590f8c1bf89410723f8523f9b0484/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:08:09Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T14:08:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix onboarding locale reverting to English after signup (#22675)\n\nDuring onboarding the UI reverted to English after email verification.\nThe chosen locale was never stored on the user, so the workspace member\nseeded from it inherited `en`, and after workspace activation\n`loadCurrentUser` reactivated `en` and flipped the whole UI to English\nregardless of the browser language.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n**Backend (the actual fix):** the `signUp` resolver received\n`signUpInput.locale` but only used it for the verification email,\ncreating the user without it (so it defaulted to `en`). It now passes\nthe locale into `signUpWithoutWorkspace`, and the SSO create-a-workspace\npath forwards `locale` as well. The user, and the workspace member\ncreated from it at activation, now keep the chosen locale, so the\npost-activation reactivation no longer forces English.\n\n**Frontend:** carry the active locale across the workspace subdomain\nredirect (in `useBuildSearchParamsFromUrlSyncedStates`) so the freshly\nloaded subdomain renders `/verify` in the right language before the\ncurrent user loads, instead of briefly falling back to the browser\ndefault. Minor, only affects the case where the chosen locale differs\nfrom the browser language.","tree":{"sha":"8d768a3fbd8b30ef3479a39928b6a315938713bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/8d768a3fbd8b30ef3479a39928b6a315938713bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/f06ba08b162590f8c1bf89410723f8523f9b0484","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d768a3fbd8b30ef3479a39928b6a315938713bf\nparent a22fdf1d8e048911b7e599f4b10e34074012fcce\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1783606089 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783606089 +0000\n\nFix onboarding locale reverting to English after signup (#22675)\n\nDuring onboarding the UI reverted to English after email verification.\nThe chosen locale was never stored on the user, so the workspace member\nseeded from it inherited `en`, and after workspace activation\n`loadCurrentUser` reactivated `en` and flipped the whole UI to English\nregardless of the browser language.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n**Backend (the actual fix):** the `signUp` resolver received\n`signUpInput.locale` but only used it for the verification email,\ncreating the user without it (so it defaulted to `en`). It now passes\nthe locale into `signUpWithoutWorkspace`, and the SSO create-a-workspace\npath forwards `locale` as well. The user, and the workspace member\ncreated from it at activation, now keep the chosen locale, so the\npost-activation reactivation no longer forces English.\n\n**Frontend:** carry the active locale across the workspace subdomain\nredirect (in `useBuildSearchParamsFromUrlSyncedStates`) so the freshly\nloaded subdomain renders `/verify` in the right language before the\ncurrent user loads, instead of briefly falling back to the browser\ndefault. Minor, only affects the case where the chosen locale differs\nfrom the browser language.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT6tJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALFIQAEmTdc9/RwRXDY74mPTZhkEV\n0IoH08tU67N6ZcOZvHncuq1qMNMPjUCnKeN7JpMuJc9/H48FLsGJ3GY3htLXQzl+\n44m2BeAbN/HC0hq7kJWh6ZZGP0GYdJpJtFZKHue/V7tPjQtZaU4JJ0rXPxe0SQ4q\nNpPKtdWNjejqd9VCq1HkU+tPaqbtIzpgDJkuAYWMTFh4etXs6bcE6995vQBYy1GX\njs24DjMMY9v2a8CBUzmUTH2OrcjC0iFhrHeKjgbsi/TD/GqHzZcuhodivvTqV+xT\naTCPbNlpZyJqFCBQbYa0Ci7pxjbgSYsFsBbzjPHmNrq8dWZ251s1FZh3KXCwxyyy\nPRFNa5FT9/vNVWqz7lucrvBqMnv2lqua8lD5rVp+obXSvgbW3E4bFwoe531iUW9l\n8Y8QOOv0Drw1ETV3YFp2OPb1Ir+04wN+DJ5xMPKwE2oUtOYYrQhikR8lO7VWwlz+\nmuY938qkyFY8fuM/S5tb4214VWrE1EdXbawbWkjj1Vsye/4kRM0lO5B8uNJvSuNm\nccNCyHmc/6UXP1jUAIom71ejulz3cLBxAsWqhwt1oCc+C7Lw2Fquxy8MmhJcqy0Q\nz6yUVAuPPyZrCgzDbFJbCoPaWtrkFHjrhzUQWTFy3twHmIxBH73BCIcEVItAd3Z5\nHvDV6GYLE486am4eoTot\n=Fxuw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:14:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/f06ba08b162590f8c1bf89410723f8523f9b0484","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKGYwNmJhMDhiMTYyNTkwZjhjMWJmODk0MTA3MjNmODUyM2Y5YjA0ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/a22fdf1d8e048911b7e599f4b10e34074012fcce","sha":"a22fdf1d8e048911b7e599f4b10e34074012fcce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/a22fdf1d8e048911b7e599f4b10e34074012fcce"}],"sha":"f06ba08b162590f8c1bf89410723f8523f9b0484","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/f06ba08b162590f8c1bf89410723f8523f9b0484"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/a22fdf1d8e048911b7e599f4b10e34074012fcce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T13:54:55Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T13:54:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: prevent duplicate junction rows from double-fired checkbox clicks in multi-select menu items (#22737)\n\n## What\n\nFixes a bug where selecting a relation from the record picker created\n**two** rows in a junction object instead of one (issue #22698).\n\n## Root cause\n\nBase UI''s `Checkbox` renders a styled `<span role=\"checkbox\">` plus a\nhidden `<input>`. On click of the span it re-dispatches a second,\n*bubbling* click on the hidden input (to keep the native input in sync)\nwithout stopping propagation. Both the original span click and the\nre-dispatched input click bubble up to the menu-item row, whose\n`onClick` drives selection — so one physical click on the checkbox fired\nthe row''s handler **twice**.\n\nThis was invisible until now because every consumer''s handler was\nidempotent:\n- multi-select toggle: both calls pass the same `!selected`, net one\ntoggle\n- relation attach: setting a foreign key twice is the same result\n\nThe junction relation feature is the first non-idempotent consumer: each\ncall creates a new junction record with a fresh UUID, so two calls\nproduced two rows.\n\n## Fix\n\nExtract a shared `MenuItemMultiSelectCheckbox` part that:\n- drives selection through the checkbox''s own `onCheckedChange` (events\nup)\n- wraps the checkbox so its click cannot propagate to the row''s\n`onClick`\n\nThe row stays clickable for the rest of the item; the checkbox click and\nthe row click are now two clean, single-fire event sources. Applied to\nall three affected components (`MenuItemMultiSelect`,\n`MenuItemMultiSelectAvatar`, `MenuItemMultiSelectTag`) so the whole\nclass of bug is fixed once, not patched per component. No change to the\nshared `Checkbox` API.\n\n## Notes for reviewer\n\n- The `oxlint-disable` for the stopPropagation wrapper''s `onClick` now\nlives in exactly one place (the shared part), following the existing\nprecedent in `OverflowingTextWithTooltip`.\n- Added a regression interaction test on the `MenuItemMultiSelectAvatar`\nstory (one checkbox click = one `onSelectChange`); it exercises the\nshared part.\n- `typecheck`, `oxlint`, and `oxfmt` pass. The Storybook vitest-browser\nrunner is currently broken locally for all stories, so the interaction\ntest was not run locally — it runs in CI.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22737?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"50e29620309404092e0a14a4e20fbc98716b8ae0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/50e29620309404092e0a14a4e20fbc98716b8ae0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/a22fdf1d8e048911b7e599f4b10e34074012fcce","verification":{"payload":"tree 50e29620309404092e0a14a4e20fbc98716b8ae0\nparent 7475b5f16fdd27030003bb69748cc92d259fd65a\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1783605295 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783605295 +0200\n\nfix: prevent duplicate junction rows from double-fired checkbox clicks in multi-select menu items (#22737)\n\n## What\n\nFixes a bug where selecting a relation from the record picker created\n**two** rows in a junction object instead of one (issue #22698).\n\n## Root cause\n\nBase UI''s `Checkbox` renders a styled `<span role=\"checkbox\">` plus a\nhidden `<input>`. On click of the span it re-dispatches a second,\n*bubbling* click on the hidden input (to keep the native input in sync)\nwithout stopping propagation. Both the original span click and the\nre-dispatched input click bubble up to the menu-item row, whose\n`onClick` drives selection — so one physical click on the checkbox fired\nthe row''s handler **twice**.\n\nThis was invisible until now because every consumer''s handler was\nidempotent:\n- multi-select toggle: both calls pass the same `!selected`, net one\ntoggle\n- relation attach: setting a foreign key twice is the same result\n\nThe junction relation feature is the first non-idempotent consumer: each\ncall creates a new junction record with a fresh UUID, so two calls\nproduced two rows.\n\n## Fix\n\nExtract a shared `MenuItemMultiSelectCheckbox` part that:\n- drives selection through the checkbox''s own `onCheckedChange` (events\nup)\n- wraps the checkbox so its click cannot propagate to the row''s\n`onClick`\n\nThe row stays clickable for the rest of the item; the checkbox click and\nthe row click are now two clean, single-fire event sources. Applied to\nall three affected components (`MenuItemMultiSelect`,\n`MenuItemMultiSelectAvatar`, `MenuItemMultiSelectTag`) so the whole\nclass of bug is fixed once, not patched per component. No change to the\nshared `Checkbox` API.\n\n## Notes for reviewer\n\n- The `oxlint-disable` for the stopPropagation wrapper''s `onClick` now\nlives in exactly one place (the shared part), following the existing\nprecedent in `OverflowingTextWithTooltip`.\n- Added a regression interaction test on the `MenuItemMultiSelectAvatar`\nstory (one checkbox click = one `onSelectChange`); it exercises the\nshared part.\n- `typecheck`, `oxlint`, and `oxfmt` pass. The Storybook vitest-browser\nrunner is currently broken locally for all stories, so the interaction\ntest was not run locally — it runs in CI.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22737?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT6gvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyvgQAGLIR4Z02sklpLXiWpQAaj7Y\nE34rN5ZgnEvjfPmnciGYG1JBoOe/YztYX6EFo/OQvJAKFGS+eK253Ewvu64QZtHY\nU2Sdn/NmRBxB17NegbHyme2sUbGjmn0wFDZ4z9l5+PXcOTLmMEf4ntLW/n7h2Wg1\ncC2NpEqUgPuLA3lEnYrjSQgUDkD8rgbxdoHOdrmilIDaNt4/hzNTC0bIIbxPztAt\noozujpBmRDZ2fcBNCnr74PvIlTwRT1p0EcUMmybSvxCDm0/FdFVJR50atJmFHlxZ\njxvMOho+n1QkUnO2Drr8h2862aRt8KQYmLvSIPo3l8Cw1VPbjnywKieZf3KUuloR\nnloaW9GIhYyJjEzo+N5Rp3mxLN2UEGXgdCa3sXpPgUPxhYiIVVoRpy96au2C/yTI\noUmoKHAiD4UnscaxPtGMd939glTVPxuPUysNYvjtW7pg3UZM5nBVsIb63g9Puola\n7eaOMKIw0pppd/odC+MSq0AkyYWEPf4adutgBcepIcEVyY5HLnCQrBuiUK4wXxaQ\nj5CDQPvKraSutC8Ld+yHwUmj1qQK5G7thzQEROaWOnJ/RKLwYEi1Syf0AgGp0vsj\nYgsAQrJ3/uUbA+U+ta6rKqVqPOLSVSEbmHJjm4szYMrj4YLSIPXJns4yMmqYAXjp\nUoa+TRio0qpQJAwQ4s89\n=N6Zc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T19:14:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/a22fdf1d8e048911b7e599f4b10e34074012fcce","node_id":"C_kwDOTYmR0NoAKGEyMmZkZjFkOGUwNDg5MTFiN2U1OTlmNGIxMGUzNDA3NDAxMmZjY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jdmott/twenty/commit/7475b5f16fdd27030003bb69748cc92d259fd65a","sha":"7475b5f16fdd27030003bb69748cc92d259fd65a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/7475b5f16fdd27030003bb69748cc92d259fd65a"}],"sha":"a22fdf1d8e048911b7e599f4b10e34074012fcce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/a22fdf1d8e048911b7e599f4b10e34074012fcce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45695613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/etiennejouan","id":45695613,"login":"etiennejouan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njk1NjEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etiennejouan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/commits/7475b5f16fdd27030003bb69748cc92d259fd65a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T13:47:54Z","email":"45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Etienne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T13:47:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(upsert) - tighten createMany upsert candidate lookup to avoid broad OR scans (#22721)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes a performance-correctness bug in the createMany upsert path where\nthe\nexisting-record lookup built an overly broad WHERE clause, causing full\ntable\nscans and multi-second latency on bulk upserts.\n\nReported via Sentry: a 100-record create*(upsert: true) request on\n_sdWorkspace\ncompleted with HTTP 200 but took ~14s. The candidate-lookup SELECT alone\ntook\n~6.7s because it fetched a huge superset of rows before matching in\nmemory.\n\n## Root cause\n\nbuildWhereConditions created one IN(...) per conflicting column across\nthe whole\nbatch, and findExistingRecords OR-ed them together:\n\n    WHERE \"cbCustomerId\" IN ($1..$100) OR \"environment\" IN ($101..$200)\n\nFor a composite unique index (cbCustomerId, environment), this is\nsemantically\nwrong: it OR''s the columns instead of matching them as a tuple. Because\nenvironment is low-cardinality (prod/staging/dev/test), the second IN\nalone\nmatched almost the entire table, forcing a Seq Scan and shipping the\nwhole\nresult set to the app for in-memory filtering.\n\n## Fix\n\nbuildWhereConditions now generates targeted lookup conditions:\n\n- Single-column unique keys collapse into one `column IN\n(distinctValues)`\n  condition (instead of N OR-ed equalities).\n- Composite unique keys produce one `(colA = ? AND colB = ?)` condition\nper\ninput record — the columns are ANDed as a tuple, and separate unique\nindexes\n  are still OR-ed together.\n- Conditions are deduplicated (robust JSON-based key, no separator\ncollisions)\n  to avoid redundant OR branches.\n- Values are now typed as string | number | boolean instead of being\nimplicitly\n  coerced to string.\n\n## Benchmark\n\nReproduced the incident with a table mirroring _sdWorkspace:\nhigh-cardinality\ncbCustomerId + low-cardinality environment (4 values), composite unique\nindex on\n(cbCustomerId, environment), 100-record upsert batch. EXPLAIN (ANALYZE,\nBUFFERS)\non a warm 500k-row / 392 MB table:\n\nMetric | OLD (colA IN OR colB IN) | NEW (targeted) | Improvement\n\n----------------------|--------------------------|----------------|------------\nScan type | Seq Scan (full table) | Index Scan | index vs full scan\nRows returned to app | 500,000 | 100 | ~5,000x fewer\nBuffers touched | ~45,455 (~355 MB) | 400 (~3.2 MB) | ~110x fewer\nExecution time | 224 ms | 11.9 ms | ~19x faster\nData shipped to app | ~322 MB | ~64 KB | ~5,000x less\n\nThe cache-independent facts are the proof: the old query returned the\nentire\ntable for a 100-record batch (the \"overly broad record set\" from the\nreport),\nwhile the new query returns exactly the matching rows via the composite\nindex.\n\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests for buildWhereConditions (single-column IN batching,\nnested\npaths, composite AND tuples, dedup incl. separator-collision safety,\nnumeric values, mixed single-column + composite OR) — 22 passing across\nbuild-where-conditions, get-matching-record-id, get-value-from-path.\n- [x] Upsert integration suites pass (upsert +\ncomposite-unique-index-upsert,\n      10 tests).\n- [x] EXPLAIN ANALYZE benchmark confirms Index Scan and bounded row\ncounts.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22721?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"fa21a6fc10e9c6404175fff821d3012bcf5e3748","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/trees/fa21a6fc10e9c6404175fff821d3012bcf5e3748"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdmott/twenty/git/commits/7475b5f16fdd27030003bb69748cc92d259fd65a","verification":{"payload":"tree fa21a6fc10e9c6404175fff821d3012bcf5e3748\nparent b2c2c2341ce4f35d20d9273104ead51796a4b5b2\nauthor Etienne <45695613+etiennejouan@users.noreply.github.com> 1783604874 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783604874 +0200\n\nperf(upsert) - tighten createMany upsert candidate lookup to avoid broad OR scans (#22721)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes a performance-correctness bug in the createMany upsert path where\nthe\nexisting-record lookup built an overly broad WHERE clause, causing full\ntable\nscans and multi-second latency on bulk upserts.\n\nReported via Sentry: a 100-record create*(upsert: true) request on\n_sdWorkspace\ncompleted with HTTP 200 but took ~14s. The candidate-lookup SELECT alone\ntook\n~6.7s because it fetched a huge superset of rows before matching in\nmemory.\n\n## Root cause\n\nbuildWhereConditions created one IN(...) per conflicting column across\nthe whole\nbatch, and findExistingRecords OR-ed them together:\n\n    WHERE \"cbCustomerId\" IN ($1..$100) OR \"environment\" IN ($101..$200)\n\nFor a composite unique index (cbCustomerId, environment), this is\nsemantically\nwrong: it OR''s the columns instead of matching them as a tuple. Because\nenvironment is low-cardinality (prod/staging/dev/test), the second IN\nalone\nmatched almost the entire table, forcing a Seq Scan and shipping the\nwhole\nresult set to the app for in-memory filtering.\n\n## Fix\n\nbuildWhereConditions now generates targeted lookup conditions:\n\n- Single-column unique keys collapse into one `column IN\n(distinctValues)`\n  condition (instead of N OR-ed equalities).\n- Composite unique keys produce one `(colA = ? AND colB = ?)` condition\nper\ninput record — the columns are ANDed as a tuple, and separate unique\nindexes\n  are still OR-ed together.\n- Conditions are deduplicated (robust JSON-based key, no separator\ncollisions)\n  to avoid redundant OR branches.\n- Values are now typed as string | number | boolean instead of being\nimplicitly\n  coerced to string.\n\n## Benchmark\n\nReproduced the incident with a table mirroring _sdWorkspace:\nhigh-cardinality\ncbCustomerId + low-cardinality environment (4 values), composite unique\nindex on\n(cbCustomerId, environment), 100-record upsert batch. EXPLAIN (ANALYZE,\nBUFFERS)\non a warm 500k-row / 392 MB table:\n\nMetric | OLD (colA IN OR colB IN) | NEW (targeted) | Improvement\n\n----------------------|--------------------------|----------------|------------\nScan type | Seq Scan (full table) | Index Scan | index vs full scan\nRows returned to app | 500,000 | 100 | ~5,000x fewer\nBuffers touched | ~45,455 (~355 MB) | 400 (~3.2 MB) | ~110x fewer\nExecution time | 224 ms | 11.9 ms | ~19x faster\nData shipped to app | ~322 MB | ~64 KB | ~5,000x less\n\nThe cache-independent facts are the proof: the old query returned the\nentire\ntable for a 100-record batch (the \"overly broad record set\" from the\nreport),\nwhile the new query returns exactly the matching rows via the composite\nindex.\n\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests for buildWhereConditions (single-column IN batching,\nnested\npaths, composite AND tuples, dedup incl. separator-collision safety,\nnumeric values, mixed single-column + composite OR) — 22 passing across\nbuild-where-conditions, get-matching-record-id, get-value-from-path.\n- [x] Upsert integration suites pass (upsert +\ncomposite-unique-index-upsert,\n      10 tests).\n- [x] EXPLAIN ANALYZE benchmark confirms Index Scan and bounded row\ncounts.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/22721?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT6aKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwPYQAF69l0UbTdPQkJkKNfjCNroj\n0f8W6c4j+XANBrdMyqGQt/jUe0Tf/FzGzjsja5u5RrxetCHteesmxtxC5aDPgdeF\ntAuOSpMKzadHvkB6n68Y3R3MV0by/XVsk+Kzisij88CjSmAhw3kJ5iPrtn0wAhDX\nv62Lrgr1iykwTo94/LGkX43qdzOHWy1WnaTf9tkVph4b5+lX/dP2sae865eBVxFD