":null,"email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"authoredDate":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","committedDate":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:39.894Z","repositoryId":1301285187,"sha":"b1923820bdb2dd5929f12f547b08793eb337122e"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:45:39.894Z","raw":[{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/2d3cfd7b6ed07680558e2a1ef247926a0015808d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:44:50Z","email":"jarrod@span-eng.com","name":"Jarrod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:45:27Z","email":"jarrod@span-eng.com","name":"Jarrod"},"message":"Report: carry bool/string ui variables as forward-filled state columns\n\nNumeric-only reports could not show equipment state such as which pump\nis running. The walk now also collects bool/string uiVariables; their\ncells render On/Off or the text and are carried forward within each\nwindow from the value last logged before it (30-day seed lookback), so a\nstate reads as unchanged rather than unknown. HMI Engine apps are\nexcluded by key prefix (display plumbing, not process data).","tree":{"sha":"966019a77745ea618d6ce9ae901346001a801555","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/966019a77745ea618d6ce9ae901346001a801555"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/2d3cfd7b6ed07680558e2a1ef247926a0015808d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/2d3cfd7b6ed07680558e2a1ef247926a0015808d","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDJkM2NmZDdiNmVkMDc2ODA1NThlMmExZWYyNDc5MjZhMDAxNTgwOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/38c0685522dfa268c486a46c06b99f6d660256c3","sha":"38c0685522dfa268c486a46c06b99f6d660256c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/38c0685522dfa268c486a46c06b99f6d660256c3"}],"sha":"2d3cfd7b6ed07680558e2a1ef247926a0015808d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/2d3cfd7b6ed07680558e2a1ef247926a0015808d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/38c0685522dfa268c486a46c06b99f6d660256c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:06:10Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:06:10Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Apply approved app icon","tree":{"sha":"384b9584642e8721628a3933c7309399b2878f28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/384b9584642e8721628a3933c7309399b2878f28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/38c0685522dfa268c486a46c06b99f6d660256c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/38c0685522dfa268c486a46c06b99f6d660256c3","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDM4YzA2ODU1MjJkZmEyNjhjNDg2YTQ2YzA2Yjk5ZjZkNjYwMjU2YzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/5547937b6f217888d92268afbc0c6b6e285744fa","sha":"5547937b6f217888d92268afbc0c6b6e285744fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/5547937b6f217888d92268afbc0c6b6e285744fa"}],"sha":"38c0685522dfa268c486a46c06b99f6d660256c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/38c0685522dfa268c486a46c06b99f6d660256c3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/5547937b6f217888d92268afbc0c6b6e285744fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:57:14Z","email":"jarrod@span-eng.com","name":"Jarrod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:57:14Z","email":"jarrod@span-eng.com","name":"Jarrod"},"message":"Report: name the CSV after the skid and the operator''s local report dates\n\nExported reports were named data_report_segmenter_<kind>_<YYYYMMDD>-<YYYYMMDD>.csv,\nwhich says nothing about which skid they came from. They are now\n<skid display name>_<YYYY-MM-DD>_to_<YYYY-MM-DD>.csv, e.g.\nSolar_Skid_11_2026-09-10_to_2026-09-10.csv.\n\n- The skid name is read from the install''s DEVICE_MAP entry for the processor''s\n  own device (display_name, else name, else the app name).\n- The dates are rendered in the operator''s time zone. The widget picks the\n  range in local wall time, so UTC dates were a day early for a UTC+3 operator\n  starting a report at local midnight. The widget now sends its browser IANA\n  zone as `tz` on generate_report; a missing or unknown zone falls back to UTC.\n- tzdata is added as a dependency so ZoneInfo resolves on the Lambda runtime.\n- The widget''s fallback filename (used only when an attachment carries none)\n  follows the same pattern.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KFPJtmNYqzGjfpLtbvtwva","tree":{"sha":"506101341a9b009e0d1a30b1cfac791ab827f5e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/506101341a9b009e0d1a30b1cfac791ab827f5e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/5547937b6f217888d92268afbc0c6b6e285744fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/5547937b6f217888d92268afbc0c6b6e285744fa","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDU1NDc5MzdiNmYyMTc4ODhkOTIyNjhhZmJjMGM2YjZlMjg1NzQ0ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/d687328fb0eec2a7d5f5a052f487f26b3ffdb3d7","sha":"d687328fb0eec2a7d5f5a052f487f26b3ffdb3d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/d687328fb0eec2a7d5f5a052f487f26b3ffdb3d7"}],"sha":"5547937b6f217888d92268afbc0c6b6e285744fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/5547937b6f217888d92268afbc0c6b6e285744fa"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/d687328fb0eec2a7d5f5a052f487f26b3ffdb3d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:56:57Z","email":"jarrod@span-eng.com","name":"Jarrod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:56:57Z","email":"jarrod@span-eng.com","name":"Jarrod"},"message":"Report: name columns by app + submodule, drop diagnostics sections\n\nPetronash reported Flow and Pressure \"missing\" from a Skid-11 report. Both were\nthere, but every 4-20mA app names its reading \"AI Value\", so the CSV had two\nidentical \"AI Value\" columns and no way to tell flow from pressure.\n\n- Headers are now qualified by the displayStrings of the app and any submodules\n  the variable sits under, joined with \" - \" (\"Flow Sensor - AI Value (GPH)\",\n  \"Pressure Sensor - AI Value (PSI)\") — the card title + row the operator reads\n  in the widget. Ancestors with a blank displayString add nothing.\n- Any \"diagnostics\" submodule is skipped (EXCLUDED_SUBTREE_KEYS). Apps keep\n  device-health readouts there, e.g. HMI Engine''s display \"Restarts\" counter,\n  which is noise in a customer process report.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KFPJtmNYqzGjfpLtbvtwva","tree":{"sha":"bd3014fa3c806cae27eb9ebe960c09d6564c2686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/bd3014fa3c806cae27eb9ebe960c09d6564c2686"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/d687328fb0eec2a7d5f5a052f487f26b3ffdb3d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/d687328fb0eec2a7d5f5a052f487f26b3ffdb3d7","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGQ2ODczMjhmYjBlZWMyYTdkNWY1YTA1MmY0ODdmMjZiM2ZmZGIzZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/25accab0684a51162a0781cca14e0cdf760ff3bb","sha":"25accab0684a51162a0781cca14e0cdf760ff3bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/25accab0684a51162a0781cca14e0cdf760ff3bb"}],"sha":"d687328fb0eec2a7d5f5a052f487f26b3ffdb3d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/d687328fb0eec2a7d5f5a052f487f26b3ffdb3d7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/25accab0684a51162a0781cca14e0cdf760ff3bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:43:04Z","email":"jarrod@span-eng.com","name":"Jarrod"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:43:04Z","email":"jarrod@span-eng.com","name":"Jarrod"},"message":"Report: period-scope the Total Injected Volume column so it ends on the summary figure\n\nThe per-pipeline running total was the on-device odometer''s LIFETIME cumulative\nfor the kind while the summary block quoted the report-period figure (E - B), so\na Skid 9 report ended its column at 67.22 beside a \"Pipeline A (report period)\"\nrow of 40.11. Both numbers were arithmetically right; they were on different\nscales.\n\n- Every row of the column is now cumulative minus the kind''s baseline value from\n  the same endpoint snapshot the summary differences against\n  (report.pipeline_period_value); _period_snapshots computes the per-app\n  (baseline, end) pair once and hands it to both the summary and the column.\n- A window that closed before end_ts gets a closing row carrying the frozen\n  total the totaliser republishes after the switch, bounded by the next window\n  of the kind and capped at the app''s own E_k - B_k, so with one totaliser app\n  the column''s last value equals the summary row.\n- Headers no longer double-wrap units published as \" (GPH)\"\n  (report.clean_units, column_header).\n- App-level tests over a fake data client reproduce the Skid 9 numbers and the\n  closed / reopened / offline-backlog / reset shapes.","tree":{"sha":"098e7f85b6c4722693f21f9cbbb7bec781c6b455","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/098e7f85b6c4722693f21f9cbbb7bec781c6b455"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/25accab0684a51162a0781cca14e0cdf760ff3bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/25accab0684a51162a0781cca14e0cdf760ff3bb","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDI1YWNjYWIwNjg0YTUxMTYyYTA3ODFjY2ExNGUwY2RmNzYwZmYzYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/cb54dce9898d200c39aae1f45df809fa3e586bc3","sha":"cb54dce9898d200c39aae1f45df809fa3e586bc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/cb54dce9898d200c39aae1f45df809fa3e586bc3"}],"sha":"25accab0684a51162a0781cca14e0cdf760ff3bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/25accab0684a51162a0781cca14e0cdf760ff3bb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/cb54dce9898d200c39aae1f45df809fa3e586bc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T00:44:01Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T00:44:01Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Report: unit-suffixed headings, Total Injected Volume rename, report-period summary totals\n\n- Column headings now append the ui_state variable''s units where present\n  (\"Level (%)\", \"Level Reading (m)\", \"Tank Volume (L)\"); columns without a\n  units attribute render unchanged. VariableRef gains a units field;\n  headers render via column_header().\n- The synthetic per-kind total column is renamed \"Pipeline Total Volume\"\n  -> \"Total Injected Volume\" and inherits the units of the total_volume\n  variable it replaces (no suffix when upstream publishes none).\n- The top-left volume summary is now scoped to the report period instead\n  of lifetime: per-app endpoint snapshots (last logged totals at/before\n  start and end) diffed before summing across apps, with a 7-day baseline\n  lookback cap, earliest-in-window per-key baseline fallback (merge_\n  baseline_snapshot), counter-reset rule (E<B -> E), and per-kind clamp\n  to 0 for repaint corrections. Labels read \"(report period)\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"848624f2976a1248e267ac8a6311ea23115bfa9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/848624f2976a1248e267ac8a6311ea23115bfa9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/cb54dce9898d200c39aae1f45df809fa3e586bc3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/cb54dce9898d200c39aae1f45df809fa3e586bc3","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGNiNTRkY2U5ODk4ZDIwMGMzOWFhZTFmNDVkZjgwOWZhM2U1ODZiYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/16cd68b91a97e487f7b49a913f54acb1c644b6ad","sha":"16cd68b91a97e487f7b49a913f54acb1c644b6ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/16cd68b91a97e487f7b49a913f54acb1c644b6ad"}],"sha":"cb54dce9898d200c39aae1f45df809fa3e586bc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/cb54dce9898d200c39aae1f45df809fa3e586bc3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/16cd68b91a97e487f7b49a913f54acb1c644b6ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T00:57:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T00:57:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Report: per-pipeline running total replaces grand total_volume column\n\nIn a per-pipeline report the \"Total Volume Pumped\" column showed the grand\nrunning totaliser across ALL pipelines, which is misleading when the report is\nabout one pipeline. It''s now replaced by a \"Pipeline Total Volume\" column: a\nrunning total scoped to the report''s own kind, read from segment_totals_json\n(the per-kind cumulative the totaliser publishes alongside total_volume).\n\nConditional on the convention: the swap only happens when the total_volume\nsource app also publishes segment_totals_json (report.find_total_volume_ref +\na presence check on the tag_values aggregate). Devices without it keep their\nplain total_volume column unchanged. The grand total still appears in the\nall-time summary block above the table.\n\npipeline_total_value reads segment_totals_json[kind] per message (0.0 for a\nkind with no volume yet, blank on diffs that don''t carry it — same row coverage\nthe grand-total column had). Verified against live staging data: a Pipeline A\nreport renders 46.13 (that pipeline''s total) in place of the 180.42 grand total.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"90146a50cf8bf73d7904212272415ed1a2b550e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/90146a50cf8bf73d7904212272415ed1a2b550e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/16cd68b91a97e487f7b49a913f54acb1c644b6ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/16cd68b91a97e487f7b49a913f54acb1c644b6ad","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDE2Y2Q2OGI5MWE5N2U0ODdmN2I0OWE5MTNmNTRhY2IxYzY0NGI2YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/ee240fc842ddafe1a329c7564f2e4364b17b81a7","sha":"ee240fc842ddafe1a329c7564f2e4364b17b81a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/ee240fc842ddafe1a329c7564f2e4364b17b81a7"}],"sha":"16cd68b91a97e487f7b49a913f54acb1c644b6ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/16cd68b91a97e487f7b49a913f54acb1c644b6ad"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/ee240fc842ddafe1a329c7564f2e4364b17b81a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T00:27:33Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T00:27:33Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Report: round all numeric values to 2 decimal places\n\nBoth the time-series data cells and the volume-summary values now render at 2\ndecimals, so the CSV no longer shows raw float noise (e.g.\n180.42295585648148 -> 180.42). Centralised in render_csv via _format_number;\nnon-numeric cells (missing values, a blank grand total) stay empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bcbcc2a97c39b68519a7f8bfe42f3f7b9c575f49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/bcbcc2a97c39b68519a7f8bfe42f3f7b9c575f49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/ee240fc842ddafe1a329c7564f2e4364b17b81a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/ee240fc842ddafe1a329c7564f2e4364b17b81a7","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGVlMjQwZmM4NDJkZGFmZTFhMzI5Yzc1NjRmMmU0MzY0YjE3YjgxYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/6ac5f7bb94077b79fa76c88fd0fe201222e2c831","sha":"6ac5f7bb94077b79fa76c88fd0fe201222e2c831","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/6ac5f7bb94077b79fa76c88fd0fe201222e2c831"}],"sha":"ee240fc842ddafe1a329c7564f2e4364b17b81a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/ee240fc842ddafe1a329c7564f2e4364b17b81a7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/6ac5f7bb94077b79fa76c88fd0fe201222e2c831/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T23:32:07Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T23:32:07Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Report: all-time volume summary block (grand total + per-pipeline)\n\nPrepends an optional two-column summary above the time-series table: the grand\ntotal volume and a per-pipeline breakdown (every configured kind + \"None\", 0.0\nwhere a kind has no volume yet). These are all-time cumulative figures.\n\nZero-config, by convention: the report scans the tag_values aggregate for any\napp publishing a running `total_volume` (grand) and a `segment_totals_json`\nobject (`{kind: cumulative volume}`), summing across apps if more than one\nqualifies (report.discover_volume_totals). When nothing follows the convention\nthe block is omitted and the CSV is table-only — generic devices are unaffected.\nThe Petronash \"Chemical Skid\" processor already publishes both tags, so its\nreports gain the summary with no per-install setup.\n\nrender_csv takes an optional `summary` list; application._volume_summary_rows\nreads the aggregate and builds the rows (report.build_volume_summary) over the\nconfigured kinds + \"None\". Verified against the live staging tag_values: the\nper-pipeline parts reconcile to the grand total (134.30 None + 46.13 Pipeline A\n= 180.42 total).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b5bd39d6ac9769ae7de25af092d882fa314f9920","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/b5bd39d6ac9769ae7de25af092d882fa314f9920"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/6ac5f7bb94077b79fa76c88fd0fe201222e2c831","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/6ac5f7bb94077b79fa76c88fd0fe201222e2c831","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDZhYzVmN2JiOTQwNzdiNzlmYTc2Yzg4ZmQwZmUyMDEyMjJlMmM4MzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/386189e57281fde37b9ad5d75007b8d1e5cc7de6","sha":"386189e57281fde37b9ad5d75007b8d1e5cc7de6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/386189e57281fde37b9ad5d75007b8d1e5cc7de6"}],"sha":"6ac5f7bb94077b79fa76c88fd0fe201222e2c831","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/6ac5f7bb94077b79fa76c88fd0fe201222e2c831"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/386189e57281fde37b9ad5d75007b8d1e5cc7de6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:45:24Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:45:38Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"chore: ruff format pre-existing drift (test_segments.py, segments.py)\n\nPre-existing formatting drift (unrelated to the report-label change) that\nfailed `ruff format --diff` in CI. Formatting-only, no behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af033a63638b148183c439dfa0c1e65105ce6e3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/af033a63638b148183c439dfa0c1e65105ce6e3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/386189e57281fde37b9ad5d75007b8d1e5cc7de6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/386189e57281fde37b9ad5d75007b8d1e5cc7de6","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDM4NjE4OWU1NzI4MWZkZTM3YjlhZDVkNzUwMDdiOGQxZTVjYzdkZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/a4c726497b16e9adc77b696ce8e05fe2fe51592f","sha":"a4c726497b16e9adc77b696ce8e05fe2fe51592f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a4c726497b16e9adc77b696ce8e05fe2fe51592f"}],"sha":"386189e57281fde37b9ad5d75007b8d1e5cc7de6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/386189e57281fde37b9ad5d75007b8d1e5cc7de6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a4c726497b16e9adc77b696ce8e05fe2fe51592f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:45:17Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T22:45:17Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Report CSV: human column labels instead of machine ids\n\nThe downloadable segment report used machine identifiers as CSV headers\n(`timestamp_utc`, `segment_kind`, `<app_key>.<var>` e.g.\n`offline_petronash_processor_1.flow_value`), which don''t match what the\noperator reads in the widget. Headers are now the labels the user understands:\n\n- data columns use each variable''s ui `displayString` (\"Flow\", \"Pressure\",\n  \"Tank Level\", ...), falling back to the variable''s key if it has none;\n- `segment_kind` -> the app''s configured Segments Label (e.g. \"Pipeline\");\n- `timestamp_utc` -> \"Timestamp (UTC)\".\n\nVariableRef gains a `label` (the displayString) alongside `column`; `column`\nstays the internal, unique key that fixes column order and matches values, so\nduplicate display names remain data-correct (only the header repeats).\nrender_csv takes the segment label; application.py passes\n`self.config.segments_label.value`.\n\nVerified against the live staging ui_state: header renders\n`Timestamp (UTC),Pipeline,Flow,Pressure,Segment Volume Pumped,Tank Level,Total Volume Pumped`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d45748f041fcd6c50371aed6787feb6a1ab07300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/d45748f041fcd6c50371aed6787feb6a1ab07300"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/a4c726497b16e9adc77b696ce8e05fe2fe51592f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/a4c726497b16e9adc77b696ce8e05fe2fe51592f","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGE0YzcyNjQ5N2IxNmU5YWRjNzdiNjk2Y2U4ZTA1ZmUyZmU1MTU5MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/a9c73bd7aa93dc1314916775a3d929a0a3986ca1","sha":"a9c73bd7aa93dc1314916775a3d929a0a3986ca1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a9c73bd7aa93dc1314916775a3d929a0a3986ca1"}],"sha":"a4c726497b16e9adc77b696ce8e05fe2fe51592f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a4c726497b16e9adc77b696ce8e05fe2fe51592f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a9c73bd7aa93dc1314916775a3d929a0a3986ca1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T04:01:18Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T04:01:18Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Ignore .claude/settings.local.json\n\nKeeps the personal Claude Code publish/deploy hook settings out of the public\nrepo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aeeb710f10e049716259aa2015c4c0b94481185a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/aeeb710f10e049716259aa2015c4c0b94481185a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/a9c73bd7aa93dc1314916775a3d929a0a3986ca1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/a9c73bd7aa93dc1314916775a3d929a0a3986ca1","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGE5YzczYmQ3YWE5M2RjMTMxNDkxNjc3NWEzZDkyOWEwYTM5ODZjYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/9d39b9dd939aa74b24377109bb431b8913803e4d","sha":"9d39b9dd939aa74b24377109bb431b8913803e4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/9d39b9dd939aa74b24377109bb431b8913803e4d"}],"sha":"a9c73bd7aa93dc1314916775a3d929a0a3986ca1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a9c73bd7aa93dc1314916775a3d929a0a3986ca1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/9d39b9dd939aa74b24377109bb431b8913803e4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T04:01:18Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T04:01:18Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"published to prod\n\nFirst prod publish (dv2): creates app id 203722254503165198. Prod uses the\ndefault data.doover.com endpoint — the staging DOOVER_DATA_ENDPOINT override\nstays scoped to staging_config, so the prod lambda_config carries no\nEnvironment block.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"34f65081c86188de5cd71c93ece671466de388b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/34f65081c86188de5cd71c93ece671466de388b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/9d39b9dd939aa74b24377109bb431b8913803e4d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/9d39b9dd939aa74b24377109bb431b8913803e4d","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDlkMzliOWRkOTM5YWE3NGIyNDM3NzEwOWJiNDMxYjg5MTM4MDNlNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/69ecc3a4c7c580a67ad3f3adf28453fbd50f8fd0","sha":"69ecc3a4c7c580a67ad3f3adf28453fbd50f8fd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/69ecc3a4c7c580a67ad3f3adf28453fbd50f8fd0"}],"sha":"9d39b9dd939aa74b24377109bb431b8913803e4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/9d39b9dd939aa74b24377109bb431b8913803e4d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/69ecc3a4c7c580a67ad3f3adf28453fbd50f8fd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T01:22:05Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T01:22:05Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: no timeline flash before deployment_config lands\n\ndeployment_config arrives async, so the first render fell back to\nextractAppConfig defaults — show_timeline_chart defaults ON — and a graph-off\ninstall rendered the timeline, then yanked it away once the real config\narrived. Render a neutral placeholder while that first fetch is in flight so\nthe wrong layout is never shown. Falls through and renders with defaults when\nthere''s no agent context or the fetch has settled (even in error), so it can''t\nget stuck.\n\ntsc clean; 78 tests; asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73cce91ba5be8f33344699376df1bfd15bb11a04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/73cce91ba5be8f33344699376df1bfd15bb11a04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/69ecc3a4c7c580a67ad3f3adf28453fbd50f8fd0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/69ecc3a4c7c580a67ad3f3adf28453fbd50f8fd0","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDY5ZWNjM2E0YzdjNTgwYTY3YWQzZjNhZGYyODQ1M2ZiZDUwZjhmZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/9236e6f8485be8e04c844aab848cc753a0eb008d","sha":"9236e6f8485be8e04c844aab848cc753a0eb008d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/9236e6f8485be8e04c844aab848cc753a0eb008d"}],"sha":"69ecc3a4c7c580a67ad3f3adf28453fbd50f8fd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/69ecc3a4c7c580a67ad3f3adf28453fbd50f8fd0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/9236e6f8485be8e04c844aab848cc753a0eb008d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T00:58:08Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T00:58:08Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: pin label + menu to the top when the timeline is hidden\n\nOnly the Change button should be vertically centred in the reserved min-height;\nthe segment note (top left) and the hamburger belong at the top. SegmentHeader\ngains a centerChange layout: label + menu stay in a top row (with the age\nbeneath) and the Change button centres in the remaining space. The card no\nlonger centres its whole content — the header fills it instead. Default layout\n(timeline shown) is unchanged.\n\ntsc clean; 78 tests; asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e1f2966cbe2cc3ed781eb61269de10e02b305f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/4e1f2966cbe2cc3ed781eb61269de10e02b305f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/9236e6f8485be8e04c844aab848cc753a0eb008d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/9236e6f8485be8e04c844aab848cc753a0eb008d","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDkyMzZlNmY4NDg1YmU4ZTA0Yzg0NGFhYjg0OGNjNzUzYTBlYjAwOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/574c7a30133f7c83a277dbcbd38d5c5595d81ba7","sha":"574c7a30133f7c83a277dbcbd38d5c5595d81ba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/574c7a30133f7c83a277dbcbd38d5c5595d81ba7"}],"sha":"9236e6f8485be8e04c844aab848cc753a0eb008d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/9236e6f8485be8e04c844aab848cc753a0eb008d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/574c7a30133f7c83a277dbcbd38d5c5595d81ba7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T00:51:30Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T00:51:30Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: reserve min height when the timeline is hidden\n\nWith show_timeline_chart off the card is barely taller than its header, so the\nhamburger''s drop-down spilled past the bottom edge and the host grew a\nscrollbar. Give the card a 200px min height in that case (enough for the open\nmenu) and centre its content vertically, so the Change button sits centred both\nvertically and horizontally. Unchanged when the timeline is shown — the card is\nalready tall enough.\n\ntsc clean; 78 tests; asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7412c3dcec0f54a6cabb4f443d6da50ddc0cfe22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/7412c3dcec0f54a6cabb4f443d6da50ddc0cfe22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/574c7a30133f7c83a277dbcbd38d5c5595d81ba7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/574c7a30133f7c83a277dbcbd38d5c5595d81ba7","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDU3NGM3YTMwMTMzZjdjODNhMjc3ZGJjYmQzOGQ1YzU1OTVkODFiYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/ba3123a250e916dc1fb6d9c03744811cfb85c79e","sha":"ba3123a250e916dc1fb6d9c03744811cfb85c79e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/ba3123a250e916dc1fb6d9c03744811cfb85c79e"}],"sha":"574c7a30133f7c83a277dbcbd38d5c5595d81ba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/574c7a30133f7c83a277dbcbd38d5c5595d81ba7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/ba3123a250e916dc1fb6d9c03744811cfb85c79e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T23:59:29Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T23:59:29Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: hamburger menu, config-gated Add, Change pop-up with Now/Select date\n\n- New top-right hamburger menu (HamburgerMenu) holding the secondary actions;\n  the Reports and Add buttons move into it (the centred button column is gone).\n  It sits in the header''s right column so the Change button stays centred on the\n  widget. Items highlight while their panel is open.\n- New config toggle ''Show Add Segment'' (Boolean, default true) gating the Add\n  menu item and its panel.\n- ''Change {label}'' now opens a pop-up (ChangeSegmentDialog) instead of an inline\n  editor: kind dropdown + ''Now'' (switch at this instant, = the old Confirm),\n  ''Select date'' (reveals a bounded datetime picker to backdate the switch), and\n  Cancel. useSwitchSegment.switchTo takes an optional atTs -> client_ts, which\n  the processor already clamps to [current segment start, now]; the picker is\n  bounded to that same window so it can''t offer a silently-clamped time.\n- DateTimeInput gains optional min/max. SegmentHeader''s compact mode is dropped\n  (its purpose — evenly spacing the old button stack — is moot now the buttons\n  live in the menu); the age returns to its row.\n\nProcessor 73 pytest + ruff clean, config_schema regenerated; widget tsc clean,\n78 tests, asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db6143b0200d34f30b7226f626517be5c88c0f58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/db6143b0200d34f30b7226f626517be5c88c0f58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/ba3123a250e916dc1fb6d9c03744811cfb85c79e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/ba3123a250e916dc1fb6d9c03744811cfb85c79e","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGJhMzEyM2EyNTBlOTE2ZGMxZmI2ZDljMDM3NDQ4MTFjZmI4NWM3OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/e0f27ff115a5fac630616c93c9ba090f2cebc49f","sha":"e0f27ff115a5fac630616c93c9ba090f2cebc49f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/e0f27ff115a5fac630616c93c9ba090f2cebc49f"}],"sha":"ba3123a250e916dc1fb6d9c03744811cfb85c79e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/ba3123a250e916dc1fb6d9c03744811cfb85c79e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/e0f27ff115a5fac630616c93c9ba090f2cebc49f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T04:25:53Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T04:25:53Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: even button spacing when the timeline chart is hidden\n\nWhen show_timeline_chart is off, the segment age (''2d 6h'') tucked into the\nheader row''s right column instead of its own full-width row, and the Reports/Add\nbutton column''s top margin drops to match the 8px inter-button gap. So Change /\nReports / Add sit evenly spaced with no orphan age-line gap between the first\ntwo. When the chart is shown, the header/age layout is unchanged.\n\ntsc clean; 77 tests; asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ad8f48a0e82dffc423f6b2f1e3a918ed97614ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/9ad8f48a0e82dffc423f6b2f1e3a918ed97614ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/e0f27ff115a5fac630616c93c9ba090f2cebc49f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/e0f27ff115a5fac630616c93c9ba090f2cebc49f","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGUwZjI3ZmYxMTVhNWZhYzYzMDYxNmM5M2M5YmEwOTBmMmNlYmM0OWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/8f5d48fe4b54db4a247323643db6a946fb57866d","sha":"8f5d48fe4b54db4a247323643db6a946fb57866d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/8f5d48fe4b54db4a247323643db6a946fb57866d"}],"sha":"e0f27ff115a5fac630616c93c9ba090f2cebc49f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/e0f27ff115a5fac630616c93c9ba090f2cebc49f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/8f5d48fe4b54db4a247323643db6a946fb57866d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T02:48:34Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T02:48:34Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Retroactive add-segment with overlap-merge + data_segments change channel\n\nFeature: retroactively set a stretch of the timeline to a kind, keeping the\n''every instant is exactly one kind'' invariant.\n\nPure logic (segments.paint_segment, +8 tests): paint [start,end] as kind over\nthe contiguous timeline and normalise — same-kind overlaps extend/combine,\nother-kind segments fully covered are removed, partial ones truncated.\n\nProcessor:\n- add_segment RPC: fetch the affected closed segments (with message ids) +\n  open segment, paint, then persist a minimal diff — delete changed/removed\n  closed-segment messages and (re)create new ones backdated to their end_ts,\n  update the open-segment aggregate. Splits the open segment when the add lands\n  inside the currently-open period.\n- New data_segments channel, created on deployment so other apps can subscribe\n  to segment-change notifications instead of the noisy tag_values. One\n  segment_change message per change is emitted on both switch_segment and\n  add_segment (change_type, kind, affected range, author).\n\nWidget:\n- ''Add {label}'' button under a re-centred ''Reports'' button (both centred, equal\n  width, matching the Change button via CONTROL_BUTTON_WIDTH).\n- AddSegmentPanel (kind dropdown + start/end pickers + Save/Cancel) in a 0.3s\n  collapsible; Save fires add_segment then refetches segment history (a\n  retroactive add deletes/recreates messages the live create-only subscription\n  can''t reconcile — useSegmentHistory now exposes refetch).\n\nProcessor 73 pytest, ruff clean, no config drift; widget tsc clean, 77 tests,\nasset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed1f83613515ff5156fba70408f46fe1bc10a516","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/ed1f83613515ff5156fba70408f46fe1bc10a516"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/8f5d48fe4b54db4a247323643db6a946fb57866d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/8f5d48fe4b54db4a247323643db6a946fb57866d","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDhmNWQ0OGZlNGI1NGRiNGEyNDczMjM2NDNkYjZhOTQ2ZmI1Nzg2NmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/a79dc1f93a74855bc431b61c912eb87e6532f0d9","sha":"a79dc1f93a74855bc431b61c912eb87e6532f0d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a79dc1f93a74855bc431b61c912eb87e6532f0d9"}],"sha":"8f5d48fe4b54db4a247323643db6a946fb57866d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/8f5d48fe4b54db4a247323643db6a946fb57866d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a79dc1f93a74855bc431b61c912eb87e6532f0d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T01:53:21Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T01:53:21Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: uniform handle grip, right-justify Reports, centre Change button\n\n- Brush handle: inset the white centre grip ~3px on all sides and round it\n  (radius 3) so it follows the pill''s curvature — the dark frame is now\n  uniformly thin including the rounded top/bottom (was flat, leaving a thick\n  frame at the ends).\n- Reports button: right-justify (was centred).\n- Change-segment button: centre it on the widget''s horizontal centre via a\n  1fr/auto/1fr grid in the header, independent of the segment label width\n  (was centred only in the space right of the label).\n\ntsc clean; 77 tests; asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e57a48a5415c069468a02a8ea1927fd0486ea317","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/e57a48a5415c069468a02a8ea1927fd0486ea317"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/a79dc1f93a74855bc431b61c912eb87e6532f0d9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/a79dc1f93a74855bc431b61c912eb87e6532f0d9","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGE3OWRjMWY5M2E3NDg1NWJjNDMxYjYxYzkxMmViODdlNjUzMmYwZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/d0b86e7ac0dfc92450a4939ddc2d1394bb823997","sha":"d0b86e7ac0dfc92450a4939ddc2d1394bb823997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/d0b86e7ac0dfc92450a4939ddc2d1394bb823997"}],"sha":"a79dc1f93a74855bc431b61c912eb87e6532f0d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a79dc1f93a74855bc431b61c912eb87e6532f0d9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/d0b86e7ac0dfc92450a4939ddc2d1394bb823997/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T01:39:20Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T01:39:20Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: config-gated chart, collapsible two-column Reports, legend + handle tweaks\n\n- Remove the in-bar segment labels from the Gantt.\n- Move the legend from between the two graphs to beneath the overview brush.\n- Brush handles: widen the white centre grip (2->6px) so the dark frame around\n  it is roughly half as thick; handle width and shape unchanged.\n- New config toggle ''Show Timeline Chart'' (Boolean, default true); the widget\n  hides the whole timeline section when it''s set false.\n- Rename the ''Generate Report'' button to ''Reports'' (open) / ''Hide Reports''.\n- Move Recent Reports into the collapsible reports section as its right-hand\n  column (generate form left, recent reports right); it no longer sits\n  standalone below. ReportList now fills its column.\n- Animate the reports section open/close with a 0.3s grid-template-rows\n  0fr<->1fr transition (true auto-height, overflow-clipped).\n\nProcessor 65 pytest; widget tsc clean; 77 tests; asset builds; config_schema\nregenerated (show_timeline_chart default true).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"99f487f06ccf8157fbf11e4b7b10904055eb896f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/99f487f06ccf8157fbf11e4b7b10904055eb896f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/d0b86e7ac0dfc92450a4939ddc2d1394bb823997","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/d0b86e7ac0dfc92450a4939ddc2d1394bb823997","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGQwYjg2ZTdhYzBkZmM5MjQ1MGE0OTM5ZGRjMmQxMzk0YmI4MjM5OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/64e7f32bb6c0c2a25e79119514b0af3879e00b89","sha":"64e7f32bb6c0c2a25e79119514b0af3879e00b89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/64e7f32bb6c0c2a25e79119514b0af3879e00b89"}],"sha":"d0b86e7ac0dfc92450a4939ddc2d1394bb823997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/d0b86e7ac0dfc92450a4939ddc2d1394bb823997"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/64e7f32bb6c0c2a25e79119514b0af3879e00b89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T00:46:25Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T00:46:25Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: match Doover graph date picker + brush styling exactly\n\nRestyle the date-range picker and the overview brush selection to match the\nDoover 2.0 graph (dateTimeRange + CustomBrush), using Doover''s own shadcn/\nTailwind CSS custom properties (--primary, --input, --border, --muted,\n--popover, --radius-*) with hard slate fallbacks so they track the host theme\nin light and dark.\n\n- DateRangePicker trigger: InputGroup style — 28px tall, 1px --input border,\n  8px radius, bg-input/20, two centred 14px date fields around an en-dash, no\n  icon (was a single panel button). Calendar popover is now anchored below the\n  trigger (Doover uses a popover, not a modal) with bg-popover, a foreground/10\n  ring + shadow-md, 10px radius; 36px day cells, --primary selected days,\n  --muted range-middle/today, muted-foreground weekday header; presets as small\n  ghost buttons and a --primary Apply.\n- TimelineBrush: selection window is now Doover''s translucent --primary fill\n  (no border, cursor move) with no separate outside dimming; travellers are\n  12px dark rounded pills straddling each edge with a white centre grip bar\n  (was thin accent bars). Gantt mini-bars unchanged.\n\ntsc clean; 76 tests; asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"66df5716860912cdea6299e958df4905fce7bf91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/66df5716860912cdea6299e958df4905fce7bf91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/64e7f32bb6c0c2a25e79119514b0af3879e00b89","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/64e7f32bb6c0c2a25e79119514b0af3879e00b89","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDY0ZTdmMzJiYjZjMGMyYTI1ZTc5MTE5NTE0YjBhZjM4NzllMDBiODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/62a219e4472cfb08d895de9f841ce75fdf9a2df6","sha":"62a219e4472cfb08d895de9f841ce75fdf9a2df6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/62a219e4472cfb08d895de9f841ce75fdf9a2df6"}],"sha":"64e7f32bb6c0c2a25e79119514b0af3879e00b89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/64e7f32bb6c0c2a25e79119514b0af3879e00b89"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/62a219e4472cfb08d895de9f841ce75fdf9a2df6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T00:40:21Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T00:40:21Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget UX: report date format, header age, move Generate Report below chart\n\n- Recent Reports buttons: drop the time, show dates as dd/mm/yy, and use a\n  plain hyphen between start/end instead of the arrow (formatDateDMY).\n- Segment header age: drop ''since'', show days+hours via formatDuration\n  (e.g. ''2d 6h'') instead of ''2d ago''.\n- Move the Generate Report button out of the timeline control row to below the\n  Gantt/brush, centred, sitting above the Recent Reports section.\n- Centre the date-range picker above the chart (control row now picker-only).\n\n+1 format test (76 total); tsc clean; asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc244fe58dacb5be5957860f16493699b1fca9fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/dc244fe58dacb5be5957860f16493699b1fca9fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/62a219e4472cfb08d895de9f841ce75fdf9a2df6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/62a219e4472cfb08d895de9f841ce75fdf9a2df6","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDYyYTIxOWU0NDcyY2ZiMDhkODk1ZGU5Zjg0MWNlNzVmZGY5YTJkZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/4b56710503a8e7f9eeeb0bf3ce0d4872621f0f9c","sha":"4b56710503a8e7f9eeeb0bf3ce0d4872621f0f9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/4b56710503a8e7f9eeeb0bf3ce0d4872621f0f9c"}],"sha":"62a219e4472cfb08d895de9f841ce75fdf9a2df6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/62a219e4472cfb08d895de9f841ce75fdf9a2df6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/4b56710503a8e7f9eeeb0bf3ce0d4872621f0f9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:57:18Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:57:18Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget UX: inline timeline controls, centered legend, restyled Recent Reports\n\n- TimelineSection: pull the Generate Report button + date picker into the same\n  75% centred column as the Gantt so they sit inline with the chart edges\n  instead of hanging off the card edges.\n- GanttTimeline: centre the legend (justifyContent: center).\n- ReportList: centre the ''Recent reports'' title; narrow the list to 25% width,\n  centred; each completed report is now a single blue button (accent bg) with a\n  white label (kind · start → end) that downloads on click — the ''Download''\n  word is gone (the whole row is the control).\n\ntsc clean; 75 widget tests pass; asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a1297ece9dcceeddbc37b137b33b755b74c3813","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/7a1297ece9dcceeddbc37b137b33b755b74c3813"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/4b56710503a8e7f9eeeb0bf3ce0d4872621f0f9c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/4b56710503a8e7f9eeeb0bf3ce0d4872621f0f9c","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDRiNTY3MTA1MDNhOGU3ZjllZWViMGJmM2NlMGQ0ODcyNjIxZjBmOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/bcbf6da4e664e1f6b683e095a5189ed3f935d8e5","sha":"bcbf6da4e664e1f6b683e095a5189ed3f935d8e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/bcbf6da4e664e1f6b683e095a5189ed3f935d8e5"}],"sha":"4b56710503a8e7f9eeeb0bf3ce0d4872621f0f9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/4b56710503a8e7f9eeeb0bf3ce0d4872621f0f9c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/bcbf6da4e664e1f6b683e095a5189ed3f935d8e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:42:37Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:42:37Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget UX tweaks: report toggle in timeline header, modal calendar, slimmer chart\n\n- Move the Generate Report / Hide Report toggle out of the entry component and\n  into the TimelineSection header, next to the date-range picker (single row of\n  timeline controls). Entry component just passes showReport/onToggleReport.\n- DateRangePicker: render the calendar as a centred modal with a dimming\n  backdrop (closes on backdrop click) instead of an absolutely-positioned\n  dropdown, so it never overflows the widget box or triggers host scrollbars;\n  drop the old outside-click ref/mousedown effect.\n- Slim the Gantt chart + brush to 75% width, centred; give the brush top margin.\n- SegmentHeader: make the Change button the primary variant.\n\ntsc strict-clean; 75 widget tests pass; single MF asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"54a085c0e686a9715a7173665d322fc7367da305","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/54a085c0e686a9715a7173665d322fc7367da305"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/bcbf6da4e664e1f6b683e095a5189ed3f935d8e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/bcbf6da4e664e1f6b683e095a5189ed3f935d8e5","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGJjYmY2ZGE0ZTY2NGUxZjZiNjgzZTA5NWE1MTg5ZWQzZjkzNWQ4ZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/d3076b956546c1ff3497b5f13938c43469ed344c","sha":"d3076b956546c1ff3497b5f13938c43469ed344c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/d3076b956546c1ff3497b5f13938c43469ed344c"}],"sha":"bcbf6da4e664e1f6b683e095a5189ed3f935d8e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/bcbf6da4e664e1f6b683e095a5189ed3f935d8e5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/d3076b956546c1ff3497b5f13938c43469ed344c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:01:18Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T23:01:18Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: single-lane Gantt timeline + brush + date-range picker\n\nAdd a bespoke timeline visualization (Doover''s built-in graph can''t do\ndiscontinuous/segmented rendering — connectNulls is hardcoded true — and only\nthe whole MultiPlotWidget is exposed to remotes, not its brush/picker parts).\n\n- GanttTimeline: single continuous lane of colour-coded segment bars (one kind\n  active at any instant), axis ticks, now-marker, hover tooltip\n  (kind/start/end/duration), legend. Deterministic per-kind colours (FNV-1a\n  hash into a palette; None muted).\n- TimelineBrush: overview strip with a draggable + resizable window that sets\n  the visible range (Doover CustomBrush equivalent, plain pointer events).\n- DateRangePicker: react-day-picker range calendar in a themed popover + 24h/\n  7d/30d presets (mirrors Doover''s dateTimeRange).\n- Timespan {after,before} epoch-ms model (mirrors customer-site). Visible range\n  is lifted to the widget and pre-fills the Generate Report range (WYSIWYG),\n  without clobbering manual edits.\n- useSegmentHistory: live closed-segment history via useChannelMessages\n  (record_type:\"segment\", field-projected, snowflake-bounded to the window)\n  + the open current_segment from the aggregate.\n- All layout/colour/brush/tick/preset math is pure in lib/timeline.ts.\n\nDeps: dayjs + react-day-picker (what Doover uses). Also gitignore/untrack\nwidget/dist (nondeterministic MF build output; publish rebuilds via\nbuild_widget_command).\n\nValidated: pure assembly run over the live 30-day dummy timeline -> 46 bars,\n0 gaps/overlaps, stable colours. 75 node tests (+22); tsc strict-clean; single\nasset builds (358 KB).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0fcb3c6bdf5bcc6acfa6214452402fb214daf742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/0fcb3c6bdf5bcc6acfa6214452402fb214daf742"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/d3076b956546c1ff3497b5f13938c43469ed344c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/d3076b956546c1ff3497b5f13938c43469ed344c","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGQzMDc2Yjk1NjU0NmMxZmYzNDk3YjVmMTM5MzhjNDM0NjllZDM0NGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/a950f9e09bd9471a713f7b2e36e9075743b4f791","sha":"a950f9e09bd9471a713f7b2e36e9075743b4f791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a950f9e09bd9471a713f7b2e36e9075743b4f791"}],"sha":"d3076b956546c1ff3497b5f13938c43469ed344c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/d3076b956546c1ff3497b5f13938c43469ed344c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a950f9e09bd9471a713f7b2e36e9075743b4f791/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:04:37Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:04:37Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Report: tag-reference-native — enumerate in ui_state, read values from tag_values\n\nReports were coming out empty. Every NumericVariable in ui_state carries its\nvalue as a $tag reference (e.g. \"$tag.app().value:number:null\"), not a\nliteral — and ui_state only republishes the UI schema, it does not log value\nhistory. The report was reading ui_state message history and finding only the\ntag-ref strings, which it dropped as non-numeric -> empty CSV.\n\nMake the report tag-reference-native (the intended design): walk ui_state to\ndiscover WHICH numeric variables exist, resolve each one''s $tag reference to\nits location in tag_values (app() -> owning app key), then read the actual\nvalue history from tag_values messages. Adds parse_tag_ref (compact\n$tag.<path>[:type[:default]] format per customer-site TAG_VALUE_LOOKUPS),\nswitches history reads + extraction to tag_values (keyed by app_key, diffs so\nper-message sparse rows are normal; empty rows skipped).\n\nValidated against live staging data: resolves flow/pressure/tank/volume vars\nto their tags and extracts real numeric rows (~1 datapoint per value per\n~15min, the tag-log cadence). 65 tests (+6: parse_tag_ref, tag_values\nextraction); ruff clean; cold-start verified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"02423dc14b64887fb0fd5eb882d9793f62b2c20c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/02423dc14b64887fb0fd5eb882d9793f62b2c20c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/a950f9e09bd9471a713f7b2e36e9075743b4f791","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/a950f9e09bd9471a713f7b2e36e9075743b4f791","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGE5NTBmOWUwOWJkOTQ3MWE3MTNmN2IyZTM2ZTkwNzU3NDNiNGY3OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/674c1257824dac12f8adc8eb1115aab46a9d015b","sha":"674c1257824dac12f8adc8eb1115aab46a9d015b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/674c1257824dac12f8adc8eb1115aab46a9d015b"}],"sha":"a950f9e09bd9471a713f7b2e36e9075743b4f791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/a950f9e09bd9471a713f7b2e36e9075743b4f791"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/674c1257824dac12f8adc8eb1115aab46a9d015b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T06:02:55Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T06:02:55Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Work around pydoover 1.9.1 tags-manager crash on processors\n\nOnce the lambda reached our code (endpoint + subscription fixed), it crashed\nwith: ProcessorDataClient.update_channel_aggregate() got an unexpected keyword\nargument ''return_aggregate''. Root cause is a pydoover 1.9.1 bug: the shared\ntags manager (tags/manager.py:768) passes return_aggregate=False when\ncommitting tags, but ProcessorDataClient.update_channel_aggregate (and the\nbase AsyncDataClient) don''t accept that kwarg — it only exists on the\ndevice-agent gRPC client. Any processor that writes a tag via set_tag/\ncommit_tags therefore TypeErrors on commit; doover-agents avoids it by writing\naggregates directly.\n\nWork around it the same way: read/write the open-segment pointer straight on\nthe tag_values aggregate (fetch_channel_aggregate / update_channel_aggregate)\ninstead of set_tag/tag_manager.get_tag. Same on-the-wire shape\n(tag_values[app_key].current_segment); with no set_tag, commit_tags never\nreaches the buggy call. Fixing this properly in pydoover in a separate PR.\n\n59 tests green; ruff clean; cold-start import verified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5fb2d6bb4a50f0f2638551a9fd66007636f4f98e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/5fb2d6bb4a50f0f2638551a9fd66007636f4f98e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/674c1257824dac12f8adc8eb1115aab46a9d015b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/674c1257824dac12f8adc8eb1115aab46a9d015b","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDY3NGMxMjU3ODI0ZGFjMTJmOGFkYzhlYjExMTVhYWI0NmE5ZDAxNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/b03513200a3ed32c34d493c6d521059d709a7152","sha":"b03513200a3ed32c34d493c6d521059d709a7152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/b03513200a3ed32c34d493c6d521059d709a7152"}],"sha":"674c1257824dac12f8adc8eb1115aab46a9d015b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/674c1257824dac12f8adc8eb1115aab46a9d015b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/b03513200a3ed32c34d493c6d521059d709a7152/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T05:08:33Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T05:08:33Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Fix: point the STAGING lambda at the staging data plane\n\nSecond root cause of the processor never producing output: with the\nsubscription trigger now correctly wired (required-array fix, 9caf6cc), the\nlambda WAS being invoked on dv-rpc — but it aborts during setup because it\ntalks to the wrong data plane. pydoover''s processor runtime defaults its API\nendpoint to DOOVER_DATA_ENDPOINT or else https://data.doover.com/api\n(production); the OAuth token-upgrade in _setup() then fails cross-environment\nagainst the staging-issued token, so the task dies before any handler runs -\nno tag_values seed, no RPC response.\n\nThe working doover_agents app carries DOOVER_DATA_ENDPOINT=\nhttps://data.staging.udoover.com/api in its lambda Environment via\nstaging_config.lambda_config; ours had only staging_config.id, so the staging\nlambda was published with the production endpoint. On publish the CLI overlays\nstaging_config.lambda_config into the payload when targeting staging.\n\nAdd staging_config.lambda_config with the staging DOOVER_DATA_ENDPOINT\nEnvironment (prod keeps the default data.doover.com endpoint). export-config\nonly rewrites config_schema, so this hand-added block is preserved; pytest\nstill 59 green.\n\nDiagnosed by A/B of the two published app records'' lambda_config Environment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa65c01841eb5c2e13273909243b5b49e939ce55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/fa65c01841eb5c2e13273909243b5b49e939ce55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/b03513200a3ed32c34d493c6d521059d709a7152","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/b03513200a3ed32c34d493c6d521059d709a7152","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGIwMzUxMzIwMGEzZWQzMmMzNGQ0OTNjNmQ1MjEwNTlkNzA5YTcxNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/9caf6cc54409bc3154ba7068ed2a2bbe9dc03922","sha":"9caf6cc54409bc3154ba7068ed2a2bbe9dc03922","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/9caf6cc54409bc3154ba7068ed2a2bbe9dc03922"}],"sha":"b03513200a3ed32c34d493c6d521059d709a7152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/b03513200a3ed32c34d493c6d521059d709a7152"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/9caf6cc54409bc3154ba7068ed2a2bbe9dc03922/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T04:44:41Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T04:44:41Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Fix: make dv_proc_subscriptions required so the deployer wires the trigger\n\nRoot cause of the processor never being invoked: the previous commit added\ndefault=[\"dv-rpc\"] to ManySubscriptionConfig, which (per pydoover config)\nmade the field OPTIONAL/nullable — it exported as type: [\"array\",\"null\"],\nx-required: false. The Doover processor deployer only emits SNS subscription\nbindings for a subscription field that exports as a *required* array (type:\n\"array\", x-required: true), exactly like the working doover-agents app. Our\nnullable field was silently skipped: the deploy log showed zero \"Creating\nsubscription\" lines, so no dv-rpc trigger was ever created and the lambda was\nnever invoked (no seed, no RPC responses, no invocation records) — even though\ndv_proc_subscriptions: [\"dv-rpc\"] was present in the deployment config.\n\nDiagnosed by A/B against a freshly-installed doover-agents processor on the\nsame device, whose deploy log DID create subscriptions; the only schema\ndifference was required vs nullable.\n\nFix: pass required=True alongside the default. required=True forces the\nwired shape regardless of the default (config/__init__.py:321), so the field\nexports as a required array AND still pre-fills dv-rpc for fresh installs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ddc8bb5aa7cea663a2056865821f304dad8c730","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/4ddc8bb5aa7cea663a2056865821f304dad8c730"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/9caf6cc54409bc3154ba7068ed2a2bbe9dc03922","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/9caf6cc54409bc3154ba7068ed2a2bbe9dc03922","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDljYWY2Y2M1NDQwOWJjMzE1NGJhNzA2OGVkMmEyYmJlOWRjMDM5MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/f814361564c187acef3e5fa71848bab363ec0169","sha":"f814361564c187acef3e5fa71848bab363ec0169","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/f814361564c187acef3e5fa71848bab363ec0169"}],"sha":"9caf6cc54409bc3154ba7068ed2a2bbe9dc03922","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/9caf6cc54409bc3154ba7068ed2a2bbe9dc03922"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/f814361564c187acef3e5fa71848bab363ec0169/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:45:31Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:45:31Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Widget: switch via Change button + dropdown + Confirm/Cancel\n\nReplace the always-visible switch dropdown with a Change button that reveals\nthe dropdown plus Confirm and Cancel. This fixes an unreachable first switch:\na bare <select> emits onChange only when its value actually changes, so when\nthe current segment is None (hidden from the options) the first configured\nkind was already the displayed value and selecting it fired nothing. The new\nflow commits an explicit draft on Confirm (initialSwitchDraft), so the first\noption is selectable on the first try; it also avoids accidental one-tap\nswitches on the panel touchscreen.\n\nAlso show the implicit default ''None'' when no segment has been seeded yet\n(spec: a freshly deployed install has the None segment open) instead of an\nem-dash / ''No open segment yet''. +4 unit tests over initialSwitchDraft (53\ntotal); tsc clean; single asset builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e5a76e2477a41c2f0ae28a21650a1e2f864d3f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/4e5a76e2477a41c2f0ae28a21650a1e2f864d3f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/f814361564c187acef3e5fa71848bab363ec0169","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/f814361564c187acef3e5fa71848bab363ec0169","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGY4MTQzNjE1NjRjMTg3YWNlZjNlNWZhNzE4NDhiYWIzNjNlYzAxNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/750aed96f0494675917dc98a62641c3bea28f2e1","sha":"750aed96f0494675917dc98a62641c3bea28f2e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/750aed96f0494675917dc98a62641c3bea28f2e1"}],"sha":"f814361564c187acef3e5fa71848bab363ec0169","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/f814361564c187acef3e5fa71848bab363ec0169"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/750aed96f0494675917dc98a62641c3bea28f2e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:45:31Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:45:31Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Default dv_proc_subscriptions to [dv-rpc]\n\nThe widget posts switch_segment / generate_report on the dv-rpc channel\n(doover-js useSendRpc), so the processor only receives them if its install\nsubscribes to dv-rpc. ManySubscriptionConfig() shipped with no default, so a\nfresh install came up with an empty subscription list and had to be wired by\nhand — and subscribing to the wrong channel (e.g. ui_cmds) silently breaks\nevery switch: the RPC lands in a channel nothing consumes, the widget waits,\nthen times out. Bake [dv-rpc] in as the default so installs work out of the\nbox. The app needs no other subscription (ui_state / tag_values are read on\ndemand). Regenerated config_schema via export-config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c15f2373c2b0ac8fb19afc17871bb16904e7190","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/1c15f2373c2b0ac8fb19afc17871bb16904e7190"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/750aed96f0494675917dc98a62641c3bea28f2e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/750aed96f0494675917dc98a62641c3bea28f2e1","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDc1MGFlZDk2ZjA0OTQ2NzU5MTdkYzk4YTYyNjQxYzNiZWEyOGYyZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/da39aa1ab618137b4770179f1abe5e35c2b9f8ac","sha":"da39aa1ab618137b4770179f1abe5e35c2b9f8ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/da39aa1ab618137b4770179f1abe5e35c2b9f8ac"}],"sha":"750aed96f0494675917dc98a62641c3bea28f2e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/750aed96f0494675917dc98a62641c3bea28f2e1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/da39aa1ab618137b4770179f1abe5e35c2b9f8ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:18:14Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:18:14Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Fix report watch: observe update_message terminal transitions\n\nThe segment_reports lifecycle was watched with useChannelMessages, which\nsubscribes with only { onMessage } and so never sees the processor''s\nupdate_message flip from Generating -> Complete/Failed (nor the attached CSV).\nAdd useReportsWatch: useChannelMessages seeds/pages history while a\nuseChannelSubscription wires BOTH onMessage and onMessageUpdate into an\nid-keyed overlay, merged over the base list by the pure applyMessageOverlay/\nmergeReportMessage (terminal status wins, attachments never lost). A ~10s\npolling fallback runs only while a visible report is still non-terminal, so a\ndropped websocket event cannot strand the UI on ''generating...''.\n\n+9 unit tests over the pure overlay/merge logic (49 total). tsc --noEmit\nclean; build produces the single concatenated asset.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a6805acb9396516ed06530abe5ed033b36dad1b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/a6805acb9396516ed06530abe5ed033b36dad1b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/da39aa1ab618137b4770179f1abe5e35c2b9f8ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/da39aa1ab618137b4770179f1abe5e35c2b9f8ac","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGRhMzlhYTFhYjYxODEzN2I0NzcwMTc5ZjFhYmU1ZTM1YzJiOWY4YWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/22bca0cff7f3eaa4575e2844c6c8dd48f1671057","sha":"22bca0cff7f3eaa4575e2844c6c8dd48f1671057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/22bca0cff7f3eaa4575e2844c6c8dd48f1671057"}],"sha":"da39aa1ab618137b4770179f1abe5e35c2b9f8ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/da39aa1ab618137b4770179f1abe5e35c2b9f8ac"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/22bca0cff7f3eaa4575e2844c6c8dd48f1671057/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:14:05Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:14:05Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Fix list_messages time bounds: pass datetimes, not epoch-ms ints\n\npydoover''s _to_snowflake (api/data/_base.py) converts only datetime\nvalues via generate_snowflake_id_at and passes ints through UNCHANGED,\ntreating them as already-formed snowflake message IDs. Real snowflakes\nare ~2e17; an epoch-ms int (~1.8e12) decodes to minutes after the\nDoover epoch, so every windowed fetch returned [] and every report was\na header-only CSV with zero closed segments and zero rows.\n\nFix:\n- report.ms_to_datetime(epoch_ms): pure, tested helper producing aware\n  UTC datetimes; all list_messages TIME bounds now go through it\n  (_page_segment_records bounds, _collect_window_rows window bounds,\n  and the boundary forward scan which funnels through the former).\n  format_timestamp_utc now reuses it.\n- Pagination cursors stay int snowflake IDs (correct as ints): first\n  page is datetime-bounded, later pages use the oldest returned message\n  id. The termination decision is extracted to the pure\n  report.next_page_cursor(message_ids, prev_cursor, page_limit), which\n  keeps the previously int-vs-datetime ''oldest == before_cursor''\n  comparison type-safe (prev_cursor is None on the datetime-bounded\n  first page and never reaches the equality check).\n- create_message(timestamp=switch_ts) keeps its epoch-ms int (that path\n  converts/accepts ms); a call-site comment now distinguishes the two\n  look-alike int conventions.\n- Grepped src/ for other list_messages/iter_messages call sites: only\n  the two fixed loops exist.\n\nTests: ms_to_datetime (tz-awareness, round-trip, value, agreement with\nformat_timestamp_utc) and next_page_cursor (empty/short page, full\nfirst page, advancing page, stuck cursor). 59 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4e43b3d83e71e84160ebc919998ea928a7f9b01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/b4e43b3d83e71e84160ebc919998ea928a7f9b01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/22bca0cff7f3eaa4575e2844c6c8dd48f1671057","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/22bca0cff7f3eaa4575e2844c6c8dd48f1671057","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDIyYmNhMGNmZjdmM2VhYTQ1NzVlMjg0NGM2YzhkZDQ4ZjE2NzEwNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/ea324713a90376c3aefd742837d249029235dbcf","sha":"ea324713a90376c3aefd742837d249029235dbcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/ea324713a90376c3aefd742837d249029235dbcf"}],"sha":"22bca0cff7f3eaa4575e2844c6c8dd48f1671057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/22bca0cff7f3eaa4575e2844c6c8dd48f1671057"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/ea324713a90376c3aefd742837d249029235dbcf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:00:10Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T03:00:10Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Fix report fetch missing end-boundary-crossing segments\n\nClosed-segment messages are timestamped at their END, so a segment that\nstarts inside the requested report range but is closed after end_ts lay\nbeyond the before=end_ts fetch and its overlap was silently dropped\nfrom the windows (e.g. A[10:00-11:00], B[11:00-13:00], C open; report\n[10:30,12:00] for B lost [11:00,12:00]).\n\nFix: after the backward page over (start_ts, end_ts], forward-scan\n(end_ts, now] in growing chunks for the first segment record past the\nboundary (pydoover list_messages has no ascending-order option, so each\nchunk reuses the backward-paging helper). Segment contiguity means only\nthat first record can straddle end_ts; the pure selection lives in\nsegments.select_boundary_crossing_segment so it is unit-testable, and\nit keeps the record iff start_ts < end_ts (compute_windows clamps).\n\nThe LOW boundary is safe as-is: a segment crossing start_ts was closed\ninside the range, so its message timestamp falls within (start_ts,\nend_ts] and is fetched; now stated in the _fetch_closed_segments\ndocstring.\n\nAdds pure-logic coverage: crossing-record selection (earliest wins,\nat-boundary excluded, non-segment records ignored) plus the concrete\ncoordinator scenario and a regression guard documenting the lost-window\nbehaviour without the crossing record.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"14679619146e972169c603898121c6eff201e682","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/14679619146e972169c603898121c6eff201e682"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/ea324713a90376c3aefd742837d249029235dbcf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/ea324713a90376c3aefd742837d249029235dbcf","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGVhMzI0NzEzYTkwMzc2YzNhZWZkNzQyODM3ZDI0OTAyOTIzNWRiY2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/cc55e0d71b740854b2e19587a2cb4c7d6d0b9410","sha":"cc55e0d71b740854b2e19587a2cb4c7d6d0b9410","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/cc55e0d71b740854b2e19587a2cb4c7d6d0b9410"}],"sha":"ea324713a90376c3aefd742837d249029235dbcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/ea324713a90376c3aefd742837d249029235dbcf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/cc55e0d71b740854b2e19587a2cb4c7d6d0b9410/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:57:09Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:57:09Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Add Module Federation cloud widget: segment switcher + report panel\n\nrsbuild + rspack MF widget (scope DataReportSegmenterWidget) mirroring the\npetronash-hmi build skeleton (shared singletons, injectStyles, all-in-one\nchunks, ConcatenatePlugin -> single assets/DataReportSegmenterWidget.js).\n\nReads deployment_config for segment kinds/label/None-visibility and the\ntag_values aggregate for the open segment; switches kinds via useSendRpc on\ndv-rpc (wire-shape verified compatible with pydoover RPCManager); Generate\nReport fires the RPC fire-and-forget and watches the segment_reports channel\nfor the job message lifecycle (Generating -> Complete/Failed), downloading\nthe CSV attachment via its signed URL. Pure logic in src/lib with 40 node\n--test unit tests; tsc --noEmit strict-clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"69a5452a1b670be789ee0ea56d77833c49ffa11f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/69a5452a1b670be789ee0ea56d77833c49ffa11f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/cc55e0d71b740854b2e19587a2cb4c7d6d0b9410","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/cc55e0d71b740854b2e19587a2cb4c7d6d0b9410","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGNjNTVlMGQ3MWI3NDA4NTRiMmUxOTU4N2EyY2I0YzdkNmQwYjk0MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/5814a987ee407f3eb71ee626007edddf612cb400","sha":"5814a987ee407f3eb71ee626007edddf612cb400","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/5814a987ee407f3eb71ee626007edddf612cb400"}],"sha":"cc55e0d71b740854b2e19587a2cb4c7d6d0b9410","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/cc55e0d71b740854b2e19587a2cb4c7d6d0b9410"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/5814a987ee407f3eb71ee626007edddf612cb400/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Add CI: lint, test, schema-validate (no image build for PRO)\n\nAdapted from petronash-hmi but drops build-image (a PRO app has no\ncontainer) and the device-base test container. Schema validation targets\n--app-name data_report_segmenter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe795474a4246fc06829f6a03b4bbfce5ab3e7eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/fe795474a4246fc06829f6a03b4bbfce5ab3e7eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/5814a987ee407f3eb71ee626007edddf612cb400","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/5814a987ee407f3eb71ee626007edddf612cb400","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDU4MTRhOTg3ZWU0MDdmM2ViNzFlZTYyNjAwN2VkZGRmNjEyY2I0MDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/7068c9007e918127b7929120c95d0b61988e91be","sha":"7068c9007e918127b7929120c95d0b61988e91be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/7068c9007e918127b7929120c95d0b61988e91be"}],"sha":"5814a987ee407f3eb71ee626007edddf612cb400","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/5814a987ee407f3eb71ee626007edddf612cb400"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/7068c9007e918127b7929120c95d0b61988e91be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Add pytest suite over pure modules + import smoke test\n\nCovers kind rules, switch clamping/no-op transitions, window\nintersection (discontinuous + open-segment clamp), variable-tree walk,\nvalue extraction, CSV assembly (sparse/ordering/filename), and schema\nexport smoke. 43 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3828e8fd6f77a1565b1d6663343e36b18b011294","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/3828e8fd6f77a1565b1d6663343e36b18b011294"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/7068c9007e918127b7929120c95d0b61988e91be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/7068c9007e918127b7929120c95d0b61988e91be","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDcwNjhjOTAwN2U5MTgxMjdiNzkyOTEyMGM5NWQwYjYxOTg4ZTkxYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/78f44cdea2f24f4edbdb915dac1ee7d7f8aeaa22","sha":"78f44cdea2f24f4edbdb915dac1ee7d7f8aeaa22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/78f44cdea2f24f4edbdb915dac1ee7d7f8aeaa22"}],"sha":"7068c9007e918127b7929120c95d0b61988e91be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/7068c9007e918127b7929120c95d0b61988e91be"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/78f44cdea2f24f4edbdb915dac1ee7d7f8aeaa22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Add doover_config.json (PRO/PUB) and sample deployment config\n\nPRO type, PUB visibility, getdoover owner_org_key, lambda_config\n(python3.13/300/256), widget wired via build_widget_command + widget:\nfields (dv_widget_url flow). config_schema/ui_schema generated by the\nexporters. Sample deployment_config screams the dv-rpc subscription.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"05b30edfc0b3e51c238e9b09f2c86372b68e9c60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/05b30edfc0b3e51c238e9b09f2c86372b68e9c60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/78f44cdea2f24f4edbdb915dac1ee7d7f8aeaa22","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/78f44cdea2f24f4edbdb915dac1ee7d7f8aeaa22","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDc4ZjQ0Y2RlYTJmMjRmNGVkYmRiOTE1ZGFjMWVlN2Q3ZjhhZWFhMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/37e99663ec8e939676c48c5cce988e1e6a9a12ed","sha":"37e99663ec8e939676c48c5cce988e1e6a9a12ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/37e99663ec8e939676c48c5cce988e1e6a9a12ed"}],"sha":"78f44cdea2f24f4edbdb915dac1ee7d7f8aeaa22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/78f44cdea2f24f4edbdb915dac1ee7d7f8aeaa22"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/37e99663ec8e939676c48c5cce988e1e6a9a12ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Add processor source: config, UI, segment engine, pure logic\n\n- __init__.handler: lambda entry via pydoover.processor.run_app\n- app_config: segment_kinds/show_none_segment/segments_label +\n  ManySubscription/Schedule/Timezone processor config\n- app_ui: single RemoteComponent (scope DataReportSegmenterWidget)\n- application: idempotent open-segment seeding; switch_segment and\n  generate_report RPC handlers; report engine over ui_state history\n- segments.py / report.py: pure, unit-testable window and CSV logic\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"33c719223aaec2351a9ab11f7a67206c33bddcf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/33c719223aaec2351a9ab11f7a67206c33bddcf8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/37e99663ec8e939676c48c5cce988e1e6a9a12ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/37e99663ec8e939676c48c5cce988e1e6a9a12ed","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKDM3ZTk5NjYzZWM4ZTkzOTY3NmM0OGM1Y2NlOTg4ZTFlNmE5YTEyZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/b1923820bdb2dd5929f12f547b08793eb337122e","sha":"b1923820bdb2dd5929f12f547b08793eb337122e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/b1923820bdb2dd5929f12f547b08793eb337122e"}],"sha":"37e99663ec8e939676c48c5cce988e1e6a9a12ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/37e99663ec8e939676c48c5cce988e1e6a9a12ed"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/b1923820bdb2dd5929f12f547b08793eb337122e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:54:12Z","email":"sid@span-eng.com","name":"Sidljackson"},"message":"Scaffold data-report-segmenter PRO app project\n\npyproject (pydoover>=1.9.1, export-config/export-ui scripts, strict\nasyncio pytest), build.sh (package.zip recipe mirroring dra_dashboard),\n.gitignore, uv.lock and the README documenting the segment model, RPC\ncontract, report semantics and the mandatory dv-rpc subscription.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01bdf5fcd955020cd930bc740ac877f40ddc919d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/trees/01bdf5fcd955020cd930bc740ac877f40ddc919d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/git/commits/b1923820bdb2dd5929f12f547b08793eb337122e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commit/b1923820bdb2dd5929f12f547b08793eb337122e","node_id":"C_kwDOTZAJQ9oAKGIxOTIzODIwYmRiMmRkNTkyOWYxMmY1NDdiMDg3OTNlYjMzNzEyMmU","parents":[],"sha":"b1923820bdb2dd5929f12f547b08793eb337122e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits/b1923820bdb2dd5929f12f547b08793eb337122e"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/data-report-segmenter/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=2d3cfd7b6ed07680558e2a1ef247926a0015808d&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A38%3A53.068Z"}');
