-divider label instead of\n  relying on text-shadow over a photographic background; dual-tone\n  focus ring visible against light or dark buttons; 44x44 clickable\n  region for the remember-me checkbox/label; aria-invalid +\n  aria-describedby wiring from the credentials fields to the error\n  message (new __FIELD_ERROR_ATTRS__ substitution token).\n- SamlLoginProviderSettings.scss: fixed inconsistent --color-danger\n  fallback (was failing AA, let alone AAA, in one spot), darkened\n  secondary text/alert colors to clear the 7:1 AAA threshold, new\n  warning-styled treatment for the server-wide scope notice, darkened\n  the focus-visible fallback outline to clear 3:1.\n- SamlLoginProviderSettings.jsx: a background refetch failure after a\n  successful save no longer tears down the whole form (previously could\n  unmount the live-status regions mid-announcement); added a visible\n  Cancel acknowledgment and a Retry action on the load-error state.\n- Added stylelint (scss) tooling: .stylelintrc.json, lint:scss script,\n  now wired into `yarn lint`.\n- Pinned strip-ansi/string-width to CJS-compatible exact patch versions:\n  @cyclonedx/webpack-plugin''s deep node-gyp toolchain pulls in the\n  ESM-only v7/v6+ releases, which Yarn Classic''s flat hoisting was\n  promoting over the CJS versions eslint/stylelint''s own CLI formatters\n  require() synchronously, breaking `yarn lint:js`/`yarn lint:scss`\n  entirely (unrelated to any module source change).","tree":{"sha":"5a0f94c26ab5df55ce48b3e293ac2c3610bc5e6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/git/trees/5a0f94c26ab5df55ce48b3e293ac2c3610bc5e6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/git/commits/5dbf92a8c42f17ba9e91d8f8d4d890433c77ddd4","verification":{"payload":"tree 5a0f94c26ab5df55ce48b3e293ac2c3610bc5e6a\nparent b4e6f32f34120f996a28c9865a28a9d7fa178bf3\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784103454 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784103454 +0200\n\nfix(a11y): address WCAG 2.2 AAA findings on the login page and settings UI\n\n- login.html: solid scrim behind the login-divider label instead of\n  relying on text-shadow over a photographic background; dual-tone\n  focus ring visible against light or dark buttons; 44x44 clickable\n  region for the remember-me checkbox/label; aria-invalid +\n  aria-describedby wiring from the credentials fields to the error\n  message (new __FIELD_ERROR_ATTRS__ substitution token).\n- SamlLoginProviderSettings.scss: fixed inconsistent --color-danger\n  fallback (was failing AA, let alone AAA, in one spot), darkened\n  secondary text/alert colors to clear the 7:1 AAA threshold, new\n  warning-styled treatment for the server-wide scope notice, darkened\n  the focus-visible fallback outline to clear 3:1.\n- SamlLoginProviderSettings.jsx: a background refetch failure after a\n  successful save no longer tears down the whole form (previously could\n  unmount the live-status regions mid-announcement); added a visible\n  Cancel acknowledgment and a Retry action on the load-error state.\n- Added stylelint (scss) tooling: .stylelintrc.json, lint:scss script,\n  now wired into `yarn lint`.\n- Pinned strip-ansi/string-width to CJS-compatible exact patch versions:\n  @cyclonedx/webpack-plugin''s deep node-gyp toolchain pulls in the\n  ESM-only v7/v6+ releases, which Yarn Classic''s flat hoisting was\n  promoting over the CJS versions eslint/stylelint''s own CLI formatters\n  require() synchronously, breaking `yarn lint:js`/`yarn lint:scss`\n  entirely (unrelated to any module source change).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmpXQh4ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3m9tAgAobkcLHz2UWYE/uZ23jaRpc0c2m2IudNQlpxTbgrem3UtciAa00OyDuRy\n0W1VXnuafvm4FXPjsYUgH1JsgAl/QgIBMuSGXrTd/KC047SFBrLYCGlsC+ZsFJKq\nsB4Oc3Kne1886RY022A7LGa5os5VFCwDvi/XeCv2CqnkbzUJ+6pGMIGnsRvcJVM4\nXuuUMTiIKrrKBGTPfc3F9fpLxzcczNUPsJ1+UDgfQQ+9DnFnlN76FhF43nhsfF9l\nD2dGHbGrQiBr/HUXpO17h79/5LjK3Iy8lvNeY40WK3dvOGASQaNMWOFIDLlvazmb\nr7uZ6I5EktzlwjRzhM3AkufO+fP+Ww==\n=tvPE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T08:38:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commit/5dbf92a8c42f17ba9e91d8f8d4d890433c77ddd4","node_id":"C_kwDOTZBEHtoAKDVkYmY5MmE4YzQyZjE3YmE5ZTkxZDhmOGQ0ZDg5MDQzM2M3N2RkZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commit/b4e6f32f34120f996a28c9865a28a9d7fa178bf3","sha":"b4e6f32f34120f996a28c9865a28a9d7fa178bf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commits/b4e6f32f34120f996a28c9865a28a9d7fa178bf3"}],"sha":"5dbf92a8c42f17ba9e91d8f8d4d890433c77ddd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commits/5dbf92a8c42f17ba9e91d8f8d4d890433c77ddd4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commits/b4e6f32f34120f996a28c9865a28a9d7fa178bf3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T08:14:04Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T08:14:04Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"test: update Cypress specs for server-level SAML login provider config\n\nThe module was reworked to fix a privilege-escalation flaw: the server-wide\nfqdn config was previously gated by a per-site permission\n(siteAdminSamlLoginProvider on /sites/{siteKey}), letting a site-admin on any\nlow-value site rewrite platform-wide SAML auth behavior. It is now gated by a\ngenuine server-level permission (samlLoginProviderAdmin, checked on the JCR\nroot), and the admin route moved from\n/jahia/administration/{siteKey}/samlLoginProvider to the site-less\n/jahia/administration/samlLoginProvider. The GraphQL API was also namespaced\n(flat samlLoginProviderConfig/updateSamlLoginProviderConfig root fields ->\nsamlLoginProvider { config } / samlLoginProvider { update } ), with siteKey\nnow optional and carrying no authorization meaning.\n\nUpdate both specs and fixtures to match:\n- 01-samlLoginProviderSettings.cy.ts: adminPath has no site prefix; all\n  cy.apollo() calls drop siteKey and read/write through the\n  samlLoginProvider.config/update namespace\n- 02-samlLoginRedirect.cy.ts: same GraphQL namespace update; no site context\n  needed since the config was never site-scoped\n- fixtures/graphql/{query,mutation}: rewritten to the namespaced schema\n\nNo changes were needed in provisioning-manifest-*.yml or\ntests/assets/provisioning.yml: this harness never explicitly granted the old\nper-site permission (it relies on the root superuser, which already has\nevery permission at every scope), so there was nothing to re-point there.\n\nVerified against a real dockerized Jahia after the module''s locale-bundling\nfix (webpack.config.js now copies src/javascript/locales into the jar) and\nthe permission/route/schema rework landed:\n- 01-samlLoginProviderSettings.cy.ts: 8/8 passing\n- 02-samlLoginRedirect.cy.ts: 3/3 passing\nFull suite: \"Full execution successful\".\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"bfd0213050be4e1a30413f83deeeb433cfc8685c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/git/trees/bfd0213050be4e1a30413f83deeeb433cfc8685c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/git/commits/b4e6f32f34120f996a28c9865a28a9d7fa178bf3","verification":{"payload":"tree bfd0213050be4e1a30413f83deeeb433cfc8685c\nparent fa28b1433aff97f28bc6e10120a400d890cab28b\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784103244 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784103244 +0200\n\ntest: update Cypress specs for server-level SAML login provider config\n\nThe module was reworked to fix a privilege-escalation flaw: the server-wide\nfqdn config was previously gated by a per-site permission\n(siteAdminSamlLoginProvider on /sites/{siteKey}), letting a site-admin on any\nlow-value site rewrite platform-wide SAML auth behavior. It is now gated by a\ngenuine server-level permission (samlLoginProviderAdmin, checked on the JCR\nroot), and the admin route moved from\n/jahia/administration/{siteKey}/samlLoginProvider to the site-less\n/jahia/administration/samlLoginProvider. The GraphQL API was also namespaced\n(flat samlLoginProviderConfig/updateSamlLoginProviderConfig root fields ->\nsamlLoginProvider { config } / samlLoginProvider { update } ), with siteKey\nnow optional and carrying no authorization meaning.\n\nUpdate both specs and fixtures to match:\n- 01-samlLoginProviderSettings.cy.ts: adminPath has no site prefix; all\n  cy.apollo() calls drop siteKey and read/write through the\n  samlLoginProvider.config/update namespace\n- 02-samlLoginRedirect.cy.ts: same GraphQL namespace update; no site context\n  needed since the config was never site-scoped\n- fixtures/graphql/{query,mutation}: rewritten to the namespaced schema\n\nNo changes were needed in provisioning-manifest-*.yml or\ntests/assets/provisioning.yml: this harness never explicitly granted the old\nper-site permission (it relies on the root superuser, which already has\nevery permission at every scope), so there was nothing to re-point there.\n\nVerified against a real dockerized Jahia after the module''s locale-bundling\nfix (webpack.config.js now copies src/javascript/locales into the jar) and\nthe permission/route/schema rework landed:\n- 01-samlLoginProviderSettings.cy.ts: 8/8 passing\n- 02-samlLoginRedirect.cy.ts: 3/3 passing\nFull suite: \"Full execution successful\".\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmpXQUwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3mCZwgAjq89q+Ckl5BCYplL7huFK2jI8aLbkrSWeTbR1qwmuXmhXYClTHv9Ulk5\nJa2MosbITnSihJmWWUAXOS3OVdctZT28YLfKp9rkSOt2VbubXn72bJR/UJJ/JWlW\nGoIlm7jL/9LjF7xIfcZ/oWuC93AuihHx+PgDiqgOmxnk6L2i3SLsYDwH0o2Hm9Q/\nNeQbt+uYbXWY4/Z6mwjsZ1qpwrlqJ0ISUPvmJLdPzkZ+DtytC++kWsQ/UKevsoiu\n7BqMYOt/015eiGW+HWD1n8nHU+Jvxi5i2OYNB77yFMJmwOm7/WxZNCFLl5aMWXVn\nbTCsIvkgZQTMI5R3LKZFbCaiWKzt5g==\n=3iXw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T08:38:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commit/b4e6f32f34120f996a28c9865a28a9d7fa178bf3","node_id":"C_kwDOTZBEHtoAKGI0ZTZmMzJmMzQxMjBmOTk2YTI4Yzk4NjVhMjhhOWQ3ZmExNzhiZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commit/fa28b1433aff97f28bc6e10120a400d890cab28b","sha":"fa28b1433aff97f28bc6e10120a400d890cab28b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commits/fa28b1433aff97f28bc6e10120a400d890cab28b"}],"sha":"b4e6f32f34120f996a28c9865a28a9d7fa178bf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commits/b4e6f32f34120f996a28c9865a28a9d7fa178bf3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commits/fa28b1433aff97f28bc6e10120a400d890cab28b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:57:50Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:57:50Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: gate SAML config by a server-level permission, group GraphQL API under one namespace\n\nTwo related fixes, both confirmed independently by security and architecture review:\n\n1. The org.jahia.community.samlloginprovider configuration (the fqdn host list) is\n   genuinely server-wide (stored via ConfigService, not JCR), yet it was gated by\n   siteAdminSamlLoginProvider, a per-site permission checked on /sites/{siteKey}.\n   A site-admin on any single low-value site could rewrite SAML auth behavior for\n   the entire platform (disable enforcement everywhere, or add an unconfigured\n   host causing a login lockout) — a privilege escalation.\n\n   Replaced with a genuine server-level permission, samlLoginProviderAdmin, declared\n   under Jahia''s built-in \"admin\" (server settings) permission node and checked on\n   the JCR root node, mirroring how other genuinely server-wide Jahia permissions\n   are modeled and checked. Moved the admin screen from administration-sites to\n   administration-server-configuration accordingly (new path:\n   /jahia/administration/samlLoginProvider), and updated jahia-depends from\n   siteSettings to serverSettings.\n\n2. SamlLoginProviderQueryExtension/MutationExtension each added a flat root-level\n   GraphQL field, violating this project''s convention of grouping a module''s\n   operations under one namespace container (as the securitytxt module already\n   does) — flat root fields from different bundles can collide by name and break\n   the platform-wide GraphQL schema. Refactored both into thin extensions\n   publishing a single samlLoginProvider namespace field, with the actual config/\n   update operations moved to new SamlLoginProviderQuery/SamlLoginProviderMutation\n   container types.\n\nAlso: SamlLoginUrlProvider.activate() now reuses HostList.parse instead of\nduplicating its comma-split/trim/filter/lowercase logic, and the siteKey argument\non both GraphQL operations is now documented as caller-context only — it no longer\nscopes storage or authorization.\n\nUpdated the unit tests for the changed permission/GraphQL surface accordingly\n(113 tests green); README/AGENTS docs updated to reflect the new admin path,\npermission, and GraphQL shape.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"066229cc72705ecd54db4baf80a58e1d3300a929","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/git/trees/066229cc72705ecd54db4baf80a58e1d3300a929"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/git/commits/fa28b1433aff97f28bc6e10120a400d890cab28b","verification":{"payload":"tree 066229cc72705ecd54db4baf80a58e1d3300a929\nparent 20ab3dd6372851fc13ae12c0be8d61e2bfbac64d\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784102270 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784102270 +0200\n\nfix: gate SAML config by a server-level permission, group GraphQL API under one namespace\n\nTwo related fixes, both confirmed independently by security and architecture review:\n\n1. The org.jahia.community.samlloginprovider configuration (the fqdn host list) is\n   genuinely server-wide (stored via ConfigService, not JCR), yet it was gated by\n   siteAdminSamlLoginProvider, a per-site permission checked on /sites/{siteKey}.\n   A site-admin on any single low-value site could rewrite SAML auth behavior for\n   the entire platform (disable enforcement everywhere, or add an unconfigured\n   host causing a login lockout) — a privilege escalation.\n\n   Replaced with a genuine server-level permission, samlLoginProviderAdmin, declared\n   under Jahia''s built-in \"admin\" (server settings) permission node and checked on\n   the JCR root node, mirroring how other genuinely server-wide Jahia permissions\n   are modeled and checked. Moved the admin screen from administration-sites to\n   administration-server-configuration accordingly (new path:\n   /jahia/administration/samlLoginProvider), and updated jahia-depends from\n   siteSettings to serverSettings.\n\n2. SamlLoginProviderQueryExtension/MutationExtension each added a flat root-level\n   GraphQL field, violating this project''s convention of grouping a module''s\n   operations under one namespace container (as the securitytxt module already\n   does) — flat root fields from different bundles can collide by name and break\n   the platform-wide GraphQL schema. Refactored both into thin extensions\n   publishing a single samlLoginProvider namespace field, with the actual config/\n   update operations moved to new SamlLoginProviderQuery/SamlLoginProviderMutation\n   container types.\n\nAlso: SamlLoginUrlProvider.activate() now reuses HostList.parse instead of\nduplicating its comma-split/trim/filter/lowercase logic, and the siteKey argument\non both GraphQL operations is now documented as caller-context only — it no longer\nscopes storage or authorization.\n\nUpdated the unit tests for the changed permission/GraphQL surface accordingly\n(113 tests green); README/AGENTS docs updated to reflect the new admin path,\npermission, and GraphQL shape.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmpXPX4ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lqzAf9EWuDmtFYqamWapWrwAcCTWoAO9gE3RKVRoduhK6DAsEl3BAXzCo2FDHE\n6r5RnMljhIV802WIXSjKnBOKvUDkp+QuWreC2LvyD2mvyVV+8qTTgb1mDWFuMvYv\n5RLKmyTRVsMFoz/ZrWdlqcan2WrmUCBRKC4Sv/0KJ1i++X3Ace+2UbgKMA1gj+E1\nRqdT+T2ISlwd3VO8opGJY9dOPCVFCx0zXP2ko+P8yi03rqCCc2WtIBXBUQXD7SiW\n9uPnuKeOrbYS3yd4TJCFWDHWtNstxzJY9Us+cSsiNd9aPJiS4tu6Jvb8l3V1rhMt\nWI3X3JCtM74hxssQ6+BlK5DpWHZ6CA==\n=o6iK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T08:38:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commit/fa28b1433aff97f28bc6e10120a400d890cab28b","node_id":"C_kwDOTZBEHtoAKGZhMjhiMTQzM2FmZjk3ZjI4YmM2ZTEwMTIwYTQwMGQ4OTBjYWIyOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commit/20ab3dd6372851fc13ae12c0be8d61e2bfbac64d","sha":"20ab3dd6372851fc13ae12c0be8d61e2bfbac64d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commits/20ab3dd6372851fc13ae12c0be8d61e2bfbac64d"}],"sha":"fa28b1433aff97f28bc6e10120a400d890cab28b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commits/fa28b1433aff97f28bc6e10120a400d890cab28b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/commits/20ab3dd6372851fc13ae12c0be8d61e2bfbac64d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:54:44Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:54:44Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"chore: ignore the whole generated javascript/ build output tree, not just apps/","tree":{"sha":"ce47545f85de606d4a6373e47c15e3ae0b7391a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/git/trees/ce47545f85de606d4a6373e47c15e3ae0b7391a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/saml-login-provider/git/commits/20ab3dd6372851fc13ae12c0be8d61e2bf