t_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T13:57:02Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"chore(deps): clear all high advisories, vitest 5, jsdom 30, CI actions v7\n\nnpm audit: 4 high / 7 moderate -> 0 high / 0 critical. The 3 residual moderates\nare ONE advisory counted per carrier path: adm-zip@0.6.0 via\n@module-federation/vite@1.20.7 -> dts-plugin@2.8.2. It has no patched version\nand a newer MF does not drop it.\n\nNo `overrides` were needed. Every declared range already permitted a patched\nversion; npm had been reusing satisfying-but-stale copies from node_modules, so\na clean resolve moved them with no permanent config cruft. That is why the\nlockfile diff is large (net -1288 lines) — the resolve was rebuilt, and it is\nthe mechanism that cleared the highs.\n\nreact/react-dom 19.3.0, vitest 5.0.0, jsdom 30.0.1, @testing-library/jest-dom\n7.0.1, typescript-eslint 8.70.0, vite 8.3.0, @vitejs/plugin-react 6.1.1,\n@types/react + @types/react-dom 19.3.0, @testing-library/react 16.3.3,\nuser-event 14.6.7, globals 17.12.0, sass 1.104.0, prettier 3.9.6.\nCI: checkout@v4 -> v7, setup-node@v4 -> v7 (three majors; both v7 action.yml\nfiles read, node-version-file and cache confirmed present).\n\nRemoves a config block that Vite 8 had silently stopped honouring.\n`esbuild: { jsx: ''automatic'' }` was dead: Vite 8 transforms via oxc, and the\nonly esbuild sub-option it still reads is jsxInject, which this repo does not\nuse. It is DELETED rather than migrated to an `oxc` block, because\n@vitejs/plugin-react 6 already sets `oxc: { jsx: { runtime: ''automatic'' } }`\nitself — an explicit user block would duplicate the plugin and could clobber its\nFast Refresh setting. Verified from emitted output rather than from exit code:\nReact.createElement occurrences = 0, and react/jsx-runtime is imported as its\nown shared MF chunk.\n\nDeleting it also fixed a real typecheck failure: with esbuild gone from the tree\n(vitest 5 dropped its bundled copy), ESBuildOptions no longer resolves a `jsx`\nkey, so tsc failed on vite.config.ts:11. `as const` did not fix it, which is\nwhat proved the key was unrecognised rather than merely widened.\n\nengines.node narrowed `>=22.12.0` -> `^22.22.2 || ^24.15.0 || >=26.0.0`. jsdom\n30, not vitest 5, is the binding constraint. .nvmrc''s 24 satisfies it.\n\nTypeScript stays 6.x: typescript-eslint 8.70.0, the latest, still peers\n`>=4.8.4 <6.1.0`. ESLint stays 9.x: eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y@6.10.2 and\neslint-plugin-react@7.37.5 are both latest and peer only `^9`, so eslint 10\nwould need repo-wide legacy-peer-deps — disabling peer checking for every\npackage to gain three lint rules. Deliberately declined.\n\n@module-federation/vite stays exact 1.20.7. The pin is documented: the plugin\nships behaviour changes in PATCH releases (1.20.5 removed implicit sharing,\n1.20.6 changed init() semantics), so a caret invites drift into a strict\nfederation contract.\n\nlint, typecheck, format:check, 27/27 tests and build all green. The host''s share\nmap still carries 4 entries with singleton, strictVersion and requiredVersion\n^19.0.0 — 4 of 4 on all three flags.\n\nNOT verified: an actual federated mount. No browser, no dev server. Given #48,\nwhere a hanging remote entry blanks the whole site, a green build and 27 green\ntests do not prove the host still mounts its remotes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"31225114010b610a67954e2ba677869d98a15429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/git/trees/31225114010b610a67954e2ba677869d98a15429"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/git/commits/913a03831062855ebb3dd35e1d55fe3a0c005b4d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/commit/913a03831062855ebb3dd35e1d55fe3a0c005b4d","node_id":"C_kwDOTZTgI9oAKDkxM2EwMzgzMTA2Mjg1NWViYjNkZDM1ZTFkNTVmZTNhMGMwMDViNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/commit/25224758b7b2bc34b1a261fba3b0b567c1edf3f3","sha":"25224758b7b2bc34b1a261fba3b0b567c1edf3f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/commits/25224758b7b2bc34b1a261fba3b0b567c1edf3f3"}],"sha":"913a03831062855ebb3dd35e1d55fe3a0c005b4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/commits/913a03831062855ebb3dd35e1d55fe3a0c005b4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13885240?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kilianmc","id":13885240,"login":"kilianmc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODg1MjQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/commits/25224758b7b2bc34b1a261fba3b0b567c1edf3f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:14:32Z","email":"kilianmc@gmail.com","name":"kilianmc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:14:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: record the cross-origin MF verification against production (#50)\n\nThe note said the console check was \"still owed against the deployed remote\nonce climb-trainer promotes to production\". Both halves have now happened —\nclimb-trainer v2.0.0 and shell v4.0.0 — so record the result instead of\nleaving an open promise that reads as unfinished.\n\nVerified 2026-08-19: kilianmc.com''s console clean from initial page load and\nclean again on opening the climb card. Load is called out as the arm that\nmatters, since a production build logs bridge failures during eager remote\ninit rather than on card open — a check that only watches a card open would\nmiss them and look like a pass.\n\nAlso records the share map read over the wire from production —\nrequiredVersion: ^19.0.0, singleton and strictVersion both true, four keys\neach — and keeps the backtick warning with it, since grepping the minified\noutput for a double-quoted value returns a convincing false negative.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"da3271adecc2357fc1c63c28020cc47603e7e8d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/git/trees/da3271adecc2357fc1c63c28020cc47603e7e8d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/git/commits/25224758b7b2bc34b1a261fba3b0b567c1edf3f3","verification":{"payload":"tree da3271adecc2357fc1c63c28020cc47603e7e8d8\nparent 1b129027495d6c48b1c81ef78dcb5d982eac3c19\nauthor kilianmc <kilianmc@gmail.com> 1787141672 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787141672 +0200\n\ndocs: record the cross-origin MF verification against production (#50)\n\nThe note said the console check was \"still owed against the deployed remote\nonce climb-trainer promotes to production\". Both halves have now happened —\nclimb-trainer v2.0.0 and shell v4.0.0 — so record the result instead of\nleaving an open promise that reads as unfinished.\n\nVerified 2026-08-19: kilianmc.com''s console clean from initial page load and\nclean again on opening the climb card. Load is called out as the arm that\nmatters, since a production build logs bridge failures during eager remote\ninit rather than on card open — a check that only watches a card open would\nmiss them and look like a pass.\n\nAlso records the share map read over the wire from production —\nrequiredVersion: ^19.0.0, singleton and strictVersion both true, four keys\neach — and keeps the backtick warning with it, since grepping the minified\noutput for a double-quoted value returns a convincing false negative.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kilian Mateo <13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhZ4pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/Z4QAJJFhfzAQNqhwpucJRxV5g0U\nHSNyG+M+7xJoW0KPnE+oZot+XOpZJturmvTiVPJolDTmYAQkjdxHiDmvzgGdQ1xc\nAt41sO+TlTa7ObK+DslKGGuD6rWbSl8xohEPKDVLHqnCc2ZzhpU3z4J4MR01fJ4r\nnq2ZJskE6aZK7r3bLfG31ncsXt5pZ9LubKZaZU4UD4mb/5QEBnTRDmADbbu9TIXO\nrWtsltCQEfkNMgGWuVglr71GCdcXi3FN37qFTWgSwBssV4bPhlw5Cer9cEs32Pbx\nNWXHakRx4AxwdAifrBqtxrv0P5k9h/YQY1R44JfME+yU+dUekSOtHiz9xJuKHeKQ\nTa6H1Bj/5x5AxlG+zzLeaBRmL48zPZxEj+t/5Lix0d61vM6xdtaa36aB5Qz22DgQ\nU7YH/D9WXMdVa3GHri6xfsC/sA0YtPjM7fP7ccHAvq1Ou1Ywsi3CA1+9z3KO5JWS\nWLD5m2l4wudmyjCcfE3HFm4nb0dIG1AIusZIj/hnIi6