ps://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kilianmc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kilianmc/portfolio-shell/commits/60f034946526fcdeaaf15586140e24122b0bfab0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T08:40:04Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T08:40:04Z","email":"13885240+kilianmc@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Kilian Mateo"},"message":"chore(release): v4.0.0 — promote dev to production\n\nShips three dev changes to kilianmc.com:\n\n- the shared React contract narrowed to ^19.0.0 with strictVersion: true (#44)\n- @module-federation/vite pinned exactly at 1.20.7 (#45)\n- the climbTrainer remote and its project card (#46)\n\nMajor, because this is the first time the host serves two federated remotes\nand because the shared-React range is now strict: a remote outside ^19.0.0\nis a hard failure for whichever container boots first, not a warning.\n\nUnblocked by climb-trainer v2.0.0 (its PR #30): the promotion gate this repo\ndocumented is cleared, and climb.kilianmc.com/remoteEntry.js now answers\n200 application/javascript with access-control-allow-origin: *, verified by\ncurl against the real deployment. CLAUDE.md''s gate note is rewritten here as\nthe general rule it always was — promote a new remote before the host that\nconsumes it.\n\nStill owed after this merges, and it needs a browser: load kilianmc.com, open\nthe climb card, and grep the console for \"Failed to bridge external shared\nmodule\". Every cross-origin check so far was local, two ports; a mismatched\nremote mounts and renders correctly, so a working mount is not evidence.\n\nVe