ithub.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catalint/telic/commit/7191d3d346d6d2456182c352619980db62610358","node_id":"C_kwDOTZa0ydoAKDcxOTFkM2QzNDZkNmQyNDU2MTgyYzM1MjYxOTk4MGRiNjI2MTAzNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catalint/telic/commit/84aebfcb17a1aacea9548976d33ddae42397cd5c","sha":"84aebfcb17a1aacea9548976d33ddae42397cd5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/commits/84aebfcb17a1aacea9548976d33ddae42397cd5c"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/catalint/telic/commit/e41a9a7a8d0a086eae7b74f96973011c1a4be6e4","sha":"e41a9a7a8d0a086eae7b74f96973011c1a4be6e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/commits/e41a9a7a8d0a086eae7b74f96973011c1a4be6e4"}],"sha":"7191d3d346d6d2456182c352619980db62610358","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/commits/7191d3d346d6d2456182c352619980db62610358"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/787730?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catalint","id":787730,"login":"catalint","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NzczMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/commits/84aebfcb17a1aacea9548976d33ddae42397cd5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T20:55:55Z","email":"catalint@gmail.com","name":"Catalin Tanasescu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T21:02:47Z","email":"catalint@gmail.com","name":"Catalin Tanasescu"},"message":"drop the payload-privacy/egress machinery entirely (D30)\n\nRemove `exposure` (the full/local/private reach class) and its `\"[private]\"`\nmask, `transform`, `strictPrivacy`, the `missing-exposure` diagnostic, and every\negress filter they drove — snapshot exclusion, persistence''s local-skip, and the\nbroadcast/post-message/shared-worker local/private gates. telic core now records\na mark and holds no opinion about where it travels; taps, persistence, and\ntransports forward every mark, and scoping is the caller''s `send`/pattern filter\nat wiring time.\n\nThe `exposure` wire field is gone; the wire reader is tolerant, so a stale\n`exposure` on an old mark is ignored (no migration). Keeping sensitive values off\nthe payload is the caller''s job (PATTERNS AP7). D30 supersedes the transform half\nof D29; issues #5/#8 dissolve with the enum. SPEC S1.5/S7.4 tombstoned, others\nexcised.","tree":{"sha":"a11415f97ca1accda9ad7d06f97f5099ff871906","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/git/trees/a11415f97ca1accda9ad7d06f97f5099ff871906"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/git/commits/84aebfcb17a1aacea9548976d33ddae42397cd5c","verification":{"payload":"tree a11415f97ca1accda9ad7d06f97f5099ff871906\nparent c7cd8ce63328024fd0ebaa28e8bf135a87ef3bfb\nauthor Catalin Tanasescu <catalint@gmail.com> 1784235355 +0300\ncommitter Catalin Tanasescu <catalint@gmail.com> 1784235767 +0300\n\ndrop the payload-privacy/egress machinery entirely (D30)\n\nRemove `exposure` (the full/local/private reach class) and its `\"[private]\"`\nmask, `transform`, `strictPrivacy`, the `missing-exposure` diagnostic, and every\negress filter they drove — snapshot exclusion, persistence''s local-skip, and the\nbroadcast/post-message/shared-worker local/private gates. telic core now records\na mark and holds no opinion about where it travels; taps, persistence, and\ntransports forward every mark, and scoping is the caller''s `send`/pattern filter\nat wiring time.\n\nThe `exposure` wire field is gone; the wire reader is tolerant, so a stale\n`exposure` on an old mark is ignored (no migration). Keeping sensitive values off\nthe payload is the caller''s job (PATTERNS AP7). D30 supersedes the transform half\nof D29; issues #5/#8 dissolve with the enum. SPEC S1.5/S7.4 tombstoned, others\nexcised.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCAAdFiEEnawDhGF2ABwcT30zeRw5g1dn8RwFAmpZRvcACgkQeRw5g1dn\n8RzqKBAAxvUA6utOn9VPJ/45Xutvsxbnq/v3qs1o3y0rb2g9QCCYRjswbAWgmIh+\n0jJfm+qrOneHAMXClRyl+JLPPL1LuiVY8VffmENQpAhpjKuzBQ0wGG+P117Oy6Zd\nSHI1HzaGIdbXhHcW6WBOWM5Po8iSq6tP9Yu2bzLD/MmFnRdRkY8liqNB9LbtKJir\nt5kazh96F/kcwmqLWBqzstnqveAwRLrk6bYqcQ7mAgyE+8I9IflZYYk88XVAm/+H\nzIqRMs+CalrD0zRVunZEA4vAg1MzsrGle2bxGBTWFr832ZJ7nLBL6xnXM1tiTTen\nd7JBuflYPTr1InhZPoo3JmuBicIZi+7cN0T/okvfc1N4MhQgpVqGElTZkiivSj/d\n8oBpApKp7cCtJrslvIXHd/0YipZuBt1yhQ9I911Iw3Npn9lH9kz9LufODJa4VGkX\nuMG+Hbf79B23vpS6b6fsks1fd7iifBgcb0EIma+Ka53exlVAOiwg4vM3GUIJprZj\nJE2wdjxz9O2dnx8H/+dtAniM2iNPf/xpEVOcTw6oYTbU5NIazKuU9vTi6d2GWoyj\nNUWZlQIDfvDdsUs2gIfnpr3FdWhskJ1xb29batsyDbl3DaFdt4ElYa2ibGoaW/9k\nl2E4m4JA3GXNURRHKUJk2EOVIlTlgpe7lFPC0bgdXjVNNQQNfV0=\n=fPsb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T21:02:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/787730?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catalint","id":787730,"login":"catalint","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NzczMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catalint/telic/commit/84aebfcb17a1aacea9548976d33ddae42397cd5c","node_id":"C_kwDOTZa0ydoAKDg0YWViZmNiMTdhMWFhY2VhOTU0ODk3NmQzM2RkYWU0MjM5N2NkNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catalint/telic/commit/c7cd8ce63328024fd0ebaa28e8bf135a87ef3bfb","sha":"c7cd8ce63328024fd0ebaa28e8bf135a87ef3bfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/commits/c7cd8ce63328024fd0ebaa28e8bf135a87ef3bfb"}],"sha":"84aebfcb17a1aacea9548976d33ddae42397cd5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/commits/84aebfcb17a1aacea9548976d33ddae42397cd5c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/787730?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catalint","id":787730,"login":"catalint","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NzczMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catalint","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/commits/c7cd8ce63328024fd0ebaa28e8bf135a87ef3bfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T18:05:23Z","email":"catalint@gmail.com","name":"Catalin Tanasescu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T18:05:23Z","email":"catalint@gmail.com","name":"Catalin Tanasescu"},"message":"refactor(core): rename redact→transform, add the data boundary (D28/D29)\n\nBREAKING: IntentConfig.redact is now `transform` — a purpose-neutral write-time\npayload→mark mapping (redaction is one use of it; downsampling/normalization/\nclassification are others), payload-only. The strictPrivacy `missing-exposure`\ndiagnostic now keys off `exposure` alone; a transform no longer suppresses it,\nsince a mapping is not a reach declaration.\n\nAdds DESIGN \"The data boundary\" — the initiative boundary''s twin: telic records\nand honors data policy, it never authors, alters, or overrides it. exposure is a\ncaller policy telic must honor and fail closed on; the identity boundary stays\nwith the caller. D28/D29 recorded (D26 preserved verbatim, append-only). SPEC\nS1.5 rewritten + S2.1 reworded. The two open exposure leaks (#5, #8) are listed\nunder DESIGN \"Risks we carry knowingly\" as known, not fixed. Docs + SECURITY +\nCopilot instructions swept to the new vocabulary.","tree":{"sha":"3889fa96273a9eaecf7616c21e71b6da8bfcf341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/git/trees/3889fa96273a9eaecf7616c21e71b6da8bfcf341"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catalint/telic/git/commits/c7cd8ce63328024fd0ebaa28e8bf135a87ef3bfb","verification":{"payload":"tree 3889fa96273a9eaecf7616c21e71b6da8bfcf341\nparent 03588b23d97c68a35cbcf1ce5a1e7753ada293b9\nauthor Catalin Tanasescu <catalint@gmail.com> 1784225123 +0300\ncommitter Catalin Tanasescu <catalint@gmail.com> 1784225123 +0300\n\nrefactor(core): rename redact→transform, add the data boundary (D28/D29)\n\nBREAKING: IntentConfig.redact is now `transform` — a purpose-neutral write-time\npayload→mark mapping (redaction is one use of it; downsampling/normalization/\nclassification are others), payload-only. The strictPrivacy `missing-exposure`\ndiagnostic now keys off `exposure` alone; a transform no longer suppresses it,\nsince a mapping is not a reach declaration.\n\nAdds DESIGN \"The data boundary\" — the initiative boundary''s twin: telic records\nand honors data policy, it never authors, alters, or overrides it. exposure is a\ncaller policy telic must honor and fail closed on; the identity boundary stays\nwith the caller. D28/D29 recorded (D26 preserved verbatim, append-only). SPEC\nS1.5 rewritten + S2.1 reworded. The two open exposure leaks (#5, #8) are listed\nunder DESIGN \"Risks we carry knowingly\" as known, not fixed. Docs + SECURITY +\nCopilot instructions swept to the new vocabulary.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCAAdFiEEnawDhGF2ABwcT30zeRw5g1dn8RwFAmpZHWMACgkQeRw5g1dn\n8RzfgBAAjQgznbiq9bfqFXnPws7hH27501w3ZPrZA+bI/rzQNAtWcGaTVNoKoHXd\nfa0gDvfX219Qqe06ZCYu30vnQ6AZhBKYJ+mp4lfSJmOMgIj1XLmhO1C/jKOuwKAA\ncFZx1GH0KPWXR7c0zSWY1p0ebFq2XiKnrpn/Fa5JzDi/Z8/zmVexwO2ESRCLRth7\nDaU5C0rGxHJu2KwbAzolZRQRs4C7fnZYKalrsyzqpivaUQSqMdiDWCmt3h2ARZRz\nssBvV+AyDho/q+Pe6iQWjKeyw0xztzjIcxmf/H6XLuwSj1Qdnla5T7XVt3nI2Erv\nLXA0eSYeNIoL2f6J6p8WwR9G2eR2muV0Q6ChiiW62QOcKRn3XzAgXTGKWSdL1a2z\nRsBnC4nugXanr7ZHkdL02gLpvxiq7UjScOnGA/AZsDD7AlH8ALnXNT/880ROe5eP\nRNezqVewURFX/u5t4T1tMYQdJ12we0V5J94PgWAqTyUhFAlj5+AGWYTSnvgfm+GN\nVg6yQkBxWsvFvwYbGsCruHAP8q5yraB17lljadO67gm/E3G5bh1NlP/hy+znI2l5\n2AsPRLG5f6P4vlEn+5KVb78DQIJnw80aW+nH/I